# sent_id = orat1.1.172
# text = Itaque quum legislator civium victum vellet simplicissimum esse, cum luxus instrumentis omnibus litteras quoque artesque partim expulit, partim coercuit et quasi custodia vinctas tenuit, Aegyptiorum in modum, apud quos narrant Graeci traditos ante decem milia annorum modos cantici neque obsolevisse situ vetustatis neque immutatos unquam esse:
# reading_translation = And so, when the legislator wanted the citizens' way of life to be very simple, he partly expelled, partly restrained, and held as if bound in custody, along with all the instruments of luxury, also literature and the arts, in the manner of the Egyptians, among whom the Greeks relate that the modes of song handed down ten thousand years before have neither become obsolete through the decay of antiquity nor have ever been changed:
# literal_translation = And so when the legislator the citizens' way-of-life wanted to-be very-simple, with the instruments of-luxury all also literature and arts partly he-drove-out, partly he-restrained and as-if by-custody bound he-held, in the manner of-the Egyptians, among whom relate the Greeks handed-down before ten thousand years modes of-song neither to-have-become-obsolete by-the-decay of-antiquity nor changed ever to-have-been:
