# sent_id = orat3.2.16
# text = qui quum Magister equitum per tredecim annos bellum cum Polonis gessisset, postquam pace facta oppressoque ordine equestri Dux Borussiae extitit, providere opes, quibus imperium nec vi nec per optimas artes partum tutaretur, famam sibi conciliare, nobilitatem sibi devincire, plebis fidem retinere, Imperatoris Romani regisque Poloniae gratiam ambire et ab invidia ordinis se defendere celanda subinde religione, de qua sese ad colloquendum sponte obtulit, formasque varias, prout res postulabat, induere coactus est.
# reading_translation = He, after having waged war with the Poles for thirteen years as Master of the Horse, and after peace was made and the equestrian order was suppressed, became Duke of Prussia; he was compelled to provide resources by which he might protect his rule, which had been acquired neither by force nor by the finest arts, to win renown for himself, to bind the nobility to himself, to retain the loyalty of the common people, to court the favor of the Roman Emperor and the King of Poland, and to defend himself from the hatred of the order, by concealing from time to time his religion, concerning which he voluntarily offered himself for a colloquy, and to assume various forms, as circumstances demanded.
# literal_translation = Who when Master of the Horse for thirteen years war with the Poles had waged, after peace made and suppressed the equestrian order Duke of Prussia became, to provide resources by which rule neither by force nor through the best arts acquired might protect, renown for himself to win, nobility to himself to bind, of the common people loyalty to retain, of the Roman Emperor and of the King of Poland favor to court and from hatred of the order himself to defend by concealing from time to time religion, concerning which himself for a colloquy voluntarily offered, and forms various, as the matter demanded, to put on was compelled.
