# sent_id = orat3.4.15
# text = tamen haec maior est et servit vitae aeternae, quod in hac regione vera de Deo notitia lucet, et ut speramus diu lucebit." Itaque propter publicam et Borussiae et gentium vicinarum utilitatem viros eruditos et insignes, qui partim grammaticen Latinam traderent atque ad puram et nativam sermonis Romani formam in scribendo, quantum fieri posset, iuventutem assuefacerent, partim Graecae Hebraicaeque linguae auctores proponerent, partim philosophiae ac mathematum initia, iusque civile et artem medicam docerent, salariis allectos esse largioribus, quam quae per Germaniam usitata essent.
# reading_translation = Nevertheless, this is greater and serves eternal life, because in this region the true knowledge of God shines, and, as we hope, will shine for a long time. Therefore, for the public benefit of both Prussia and the neighboring nations, learned and distinguished men, who were to teach partly Latin grammar and accustom the youth, as far as possible, to the pure and native form of the Roman language in writing, partly to expound the authors of the Greek and Hebrew languages, partly to teach the elements of philosophy and mathematics, civil law, and the medical art, were attracted by salaries more generous than those which were customary throughout Germany.
# literal_translation = Nevertheless this greater is and serves life eternal, because in this region true about God knowledge shines, and as we-hope long will-shine. Therefore on-account-of public and of-Prussia and of-nations neighboring benefit men learned and distinguished, who partly grammar Latin might-teach and to pure and native of-speech Roman form in writing, as-much-as might-be-done, youth might-accustom, partly Greek and-Hebrew language authors might-expound, partly of-philosophy and of-mathematics elements, law civil and art medical might-teach, by-salaries attracted to-have-been more-generous, than which through Germany customary were.
