# sent_id = orat4.2.1
# text = Et primum ne exponam, quibus initiis causisque, postquam labe temporum et ruina civitatium, ingruente paullatim tyrannide funesta, qua non modo corpora, sed animi ipsi vincti et constricti tenebantur, mox populorum barbarorum incursionibus litterarum apud veteres flos laetissimus exstinctus est, universitates scholarum, ut Britannos omittam, in Gallia Italiaque ac deinceps in Germania extiterint renatisque litteris incrementa ceperint, caliginem mentibus dispulerint, religionis purioris fontes aperuerint lucemque disseminarint, postremo doctrinas plurimas sedulo excoluerint:
# reading_translation = And first, I shall not set forth by what beginnings and causes, after the decay of times and the ruin of states, while a deadly tyranny gradually encroached, by which not only bodies but even minds themselves were held bound and constrained, and soon by the incursions of barbarous peoples the most flourishing flower of literature among the ancients was extinguished, the universities of scholars—to omit the Britons—arose in Gaul and Italy and then in Germany, and with letters reborn took growth, dispelled the darkness from minds, opened the purer springs of religion, and spread abroad the light, and finally diligently cultivated very many branches of learning:
# literal_translation = And first not may-I-set-forth by-what beginnings and-causes, after the-decay of-times and the-ruin of-states, with-deadly-tyranny gradually-encroaching, by-which not only bodies but minds themselves bound and-constrained were-held, soon by-incursions of-barbarous-peoples the-flower most-flourishing of-literature among-the-ancients was-extinguished, the-universities of-scholars, as Britons I-may-omit, in Gaul and-Italy and-then in Germany arose and-with-letters-reborn growths took, darkness from-minds dispelled, the-purer springs of-religion opened and-light spread-abroad, finally doctrines very-many diligently cultivated:
# generator = deepseek-chat
