# sent_id = orat4.2.2
# text = neminem mihi arbitror adversarium fore, si nostra aetate universitates dixerim scholas potissimas aut esse aut esse debere, in quibus ut parentes ad liberos vitam, sic eruditionem solidam et scientiam pro saeculi cuiusque habitu quantum fieri potest absolutam doctores in suo genere perfecti ad progeniem adolescentem propagent.
# reading_translation = I think no one will be my opponent, if I say that in our age universities are either the most important schools or ought to be so, in which, just as parents transmit life to their children, so teachers, perfect in their own kind, transmit solid learning and knowledge, as complete as possible according to the character of each age, to the growing offspring.
