# sent_id = orat4.2.11
# text = Quapropter istos merito contemnimus nec vere eruditos iudicamus, qui aut dignitatem doctrinarum unice ex usu vitae quotidianae existimant, aut panis et parandi victus causa litteris operam dant, aut interiore cognitione neglecta res vulgares, quas oculis spectes digitisve contingas, quasi per manus tradunt, altioremque omnem et paullo abstrusiorem naturae seu divinae sive humanae indagationem non solum vanam censent, verum etiam reddere suspectam conantur.
# reading_translation = Therefore we rightly despise those people and do not judge them to be truly learned, who either estimate the dignity of the disciplines solely from the use of everyday life, or devote themselves to literature for the sake of bread and preparing a livelihood, or, neglecting deeper knowledge, hand over common things, which you may behold with your eyes or touch with your fingers, as it were from hand to hand, and not only deem every higher and somewhat more recondite investigation of nature, whether divine or human, to be vain, but even try to render it suspect.
# literal_translation = Therefore those-people deservedly we-despise and not truly learned we-judge, who either the-dignity of-disciplines solely from-the-use of-life everyday they-estimate, or of-bread and of-preparing a-livelihood for-the-sake-of to-literature effort they-give, or with-interior knowledge neglected things common, which with-eyes you-may-behold with-fingers-or you-may-touch, as-if through hands they-hand-over, and higher every and somewhat more-recondite of-nature whether divine or human investigation not-only vain they-judge, but-even to-render suspect they-try.
