# sent_id = orat5.1.8
# text = Me vero, cui honos amplissimus obtigerit, ut in suggestu hoc publice orator Senatus constituerer, si sollemnibus his sanctissimis mea voce celebrandis hodie quartum accinctus, ut illud, quod significavi, seu vitium sive incommodum devitem, a Rege nostris praeconiis longe superiore aliquantum discessero, haec una excusatio satis tuebitur, quod Plinius Traianum semel laudavit.
# reading_translation = But as for me, to whom the highest honor has fallen, that I should be publicly appointed as the Senate's orator on this platform, if today, for the fourth time, having girded myself for celebrating these most sacred solemnities with my voice, I should depart somewhat from the King, who is far superior to our proclamations, in order to avoid that which I have indicated, whether it be a fault or a disadvantage, this one excuse will sufficiently protect me: that Pliny praised Trajan only once.
