# sent_id = orat5.1.11
# text = In quo argumento sane praeclaro, quamvis perspiciam nihil a me aut exquisitius aut reconditius dici posse, quin tot tam diligentium scriptorum sit industria sollertiaque exhaustum, tamen eo versor libentius, quod illud non solum studiis meis, verum etiam litteris ipsis et institutionis publicae rationi coniunctissimum esse intelligo, vobisque omnibus, vel iis qui Lutheri disciplinae addicti non sunt, spero haud ingratum futurum.
# reading_translation = In this truly excellent subject, although I perceive that nothing can be said by me either more refined or more recondite, since the industry and skill of so many diligent writers has exhausted it, nevertheless I engage in it the more willingly, because I understand that it is most closely connected not only with my studies, but also with literature itself and with the system of public education, and I hope that it will be not at all unwelcome to all of you, even to those who are not devoted to Luther's doctrine.
# literal_translation = In which subject truly excellent, although I-perceive nothing by me either more-refined or more-recondite to-be-able-to-be-said, since the-industry and-skill of-so-many of-diligent writers has-exhausted, nevertheless in-it I-engage more-willingly, because that not-only to-my-studies, but-also to-literature itself and to-the-system of-public-education most-closely-connected to-be I-understand, and-to-all-of-you, even to-those who to-Luther's discipline devoted not-are, I-hope not-at-all unwelcome to-be-about-to-be.
