# sent_id = orat5.2.8
# text = Quodsi ecclesiae ministri artes liberales diligenter coluissent, ingenia studiis praestantissimis formassent, aluissent, exercuissent, profecto neque institutiones divinae tot humanis placitis exornatae, tot praestigiis fucatae et oneratae, denique formulis tam molestis conclusae et constrictae essent, nec mortales quum ad libertatem nati, tum ex superstitionis vinculis Christi ipsius disciplina vindicati novam et intolerandam servitutem animorum subissent, qua eos neque scholae iam a Carolo Magno instauratae, nec scholastici philosophi opinionibus receptis partem maximam capti exsolvere potuerunt.
# reading_translation = But if the ministers of the church had diligently cultivated the liberal arts, had formed, nourished, and exercised their talents with the most excellent studies, then indeed neither would the divine institutions have been adorned with so many human opinions, smeared and burdened with so many tricks, and finally enclosed and constrained by such troublesome formulas, nor would mortals, who were born for liberty and moreover freed from the bonds of superstition by the discipline of Christ himself, have undergone a new and intolerable servitude of minds, from which neither the schools already restored by Charlemagne nor the scholastic philosophers, for the most part captured by received opinions, were able to free them.
# literal_translation = But-if the ministers of-the-church the liberal arts diligently had-cultivated, talents with-studies most-excellent had-formed, had-nourished, had-exercised, indeed neither the-institutions divine with-so-many human opinions adorned, with-so-many tricks smeared and burdened, finally with-formulas so troublesome enclosed and constrained would-be, nor mortals since to-liberty born, then from-the-bonds of-superstition by-the-discipline of-Christ himself freed a-new and intolerable servitude of-minds had-undergone, by-which them neither the-schools already by-Charles the-Great restored, nor the-scholastic philosophers with-opinions received for-the-greatest-part captured to-free were-able.
