# text = Et excudendorum librorum artem Pontificibus ipsis esse damnosam visam, in illa praesertim scribentium licentia multo quam nunc maiore, videas ex edictis, quibus dicendi ac sentiendi libertatem in ipsa Germania, ob scripta quaedam apud Magdeburgenses, Agrippinenses, Treveros, Maguntinos divulgata iam saeculo quinto decimo exeunte callidius quam rectius sunt coercere conati.
# reading_translation = And that the art of printing books was seen as harmful by the Pontiffs themselves, especially in that much greater license of writers than now, you may see from the edicts by which they attempted to restrain the freedom of speech and thought in Germany itself, on account of certain writings published among the Magdeburgers, the Cologne people, the Treveri, and the Mainz people, already at the end of the fifteenth century, more cunningly than rightly.
