# text = Iam autem quum sacerdotum et monachorum inertia, luxus, avaritia, libido omnium adspectui paterent, in ipso Concilio Lateranensi Ioannis Francisci Pici oratione luculenter descripta, quum praeterea Germanorum principes tributa a Pontifice exacta ferrent aegerrime, ac summis ecclesiae magistratibus Deum Christianorum Iove, Christum Apolline et Aesculapio, Matrem Virginem Diana non potiores haberi testimoniis locupletibus constaret:
# reading_translation = Now, since the idleness, luxury, avarice, and lust of the priests and monks lay open to the sight of all, being vividly described in the very Lateran Council in the speech of Giovanni Francesco Pico; and since, moreover, the German princes bore with the greatest indignation the tributes exacted by the Pope, and it was established by abundant testimonies that the Christians did not hold God to be more powerful than Jupiter, Christ than Apollo and Aesculapius, and the Virgin Mother than Diana:
