# sent_id = orat6.1.1
# text = Recurrente hoc die exoptatissimo mihi et vobis omnibus, viri excellentissimi, illustres, generosi, collegae gravissimi, commilitones imprimis cari, nulli huius regni civitati quam nostrae doctrinarum scholae gratius accidere potest, quod hic dies totus sollemnibus dari et dicari solet, quibus Regem potentissimum nobis divinitus donatum summa cum laetitia celebremus, beneficia ab illo rei publicae collata praedicemus, postremo pia pro illius salute et futuro imperio vota suscipiamus:
# reading_translation = As this day, so greatly desired by me and by all of you, most excellent men, illustrious, noble, most weighty colleagues, and especially dear fellow students, returns, it cannot happen to any city of this kingdom more pleasantly than to our school of learning, that this whole day is accustomed to be given and dedicated to the solemnities, by which we celebrate with the greatest joy the most powerful King given to us by divine providence, proclaim the benefits conferred by him upon the state, and finally offer pious vows for his health and future reign:
# literal_translation = Returning this day most-desired to-me and to-you all, men most-excellent, illustrious, noble, colleagues most-weighty, fellow-students especially dear, to-no city of-this kingdom than to-our school-of-learning more-pleasantly can-it-happen, that this day whole to-solemnities to-be-given and to-be-dedicated is-accustomed, by-which King most-powerful to-us divinely-given with-greatest joy we-may-celebrate, benefits by-him to-the-state conferred we-may-proclaim, finally pious for-his health and future reign vows we-may-offer:
