# sent_id = orat6.5.6
# text = Etenim ei rei, quam primo loco posui, litteras non inservire, vel hinc intelligitur, quod scientiam quisque non extrinsecus addiscere, sed non nisi ex suo animo haurire et quasi explicare perito magistro duce potest, quodque scientiae et litterarum vis ac potestas non in rerum quotidianarum memoria et traditione, neque in quadam secundum leges praestitutas agendi facultate posita est, sed in liberali et interiore et ex ipsis principiis deducenda rerum divinarum et humanarum cognitione.
# reading_translation = And indeed, that literature is not subservient to that thing which I placed first, is understood even from this: that each person cannot learn knowledge from outside, but can only draw it from his own mind and, as it were, unfold it with a skilled teacher as guide, and that the force and power of knowledge and literature is not placed in the memory and tradition of everyday things, nor in a certain ability to act according to prescribed laws, but in a liberal, inner, and from the very principles to be derived cognition of divine and human things.
# literal_translation = And indeed, to that thing, which in first place I placed, literature not to serve, even from this is understood, because knowledge each person not from outside to learn, but not unless from his own mind to draw and as it were to unfold with skilled teacher as guide is able, and because of knowledge and of literature the force and power not in of everyday things memory and tradition, nor in a certain according to laws prescribed ability to act is placed, but in liberal and inner and from the very principles to be derived of divine and human things cognition.
# generator = deepseek-chat
