# text = Ita factum est, ut doctrinae, quarum olim seminibus sacerdotum collegia rem publicam ipsam rexerant, imminuta sacerdotali auctoritate a deorum ministeriis segregatae quasi liberae vagarentur, nec quum divinarum rerum institutio universa in caerimoniis partim sacrificulorum partim familiarum curae traditis versaretur, publica vero disciplina solam musicen et corporis exercitationem comprehenderet, publicis impensis adiuvarentur:
# reading_translation = Thus it came about that the sciences, which once by the seeds of the priests' colleges had governed the state itself, after the priestly authority was diminished, being separated from the ministries of the gods, wandered about as if free, and since the whole institution of divine matters was occupied with ceremonies, partly entrusted to the care of sacrificers and partly to that of families, while the public discipline embraced only music and bodily exercise, they were not aided by public expenditures.
