# sent_id = orat7.3.3
# text = Quod genus eruditionis quia omnibus recte educatis debet commune esse, sicut Aristoteles de musicae studio iudicavit, ita de omnibus fere liberalis institutionis partibus statuendum est, ut liberaliter eruditus, nisi artem factitare constituerit, in earum nulla iuxta quam qui illam disciplinam profiteatur, excellere ceterosque superare debeat, sed cunctis aequabili quodam modulo imbutus et ad laetum quendam pulchrumque animi et corporis virium universarum concentum formatus sit:
# reading_translation = Because this kind of learning ought to be common to all who are properly educated, just as Aristotle judged concerning the study of music, so it must be determined concerning almost all parts of liberal education, that a liberally educated person, unless he has decided to practice an art professionally, should not be required to excel in any one of them and surpass others to the extent that one who professes that discipline does, but rather, imbued with a certain even measure of all things and formed to a certain joyful and beautiful harmony of the mind and of all the powers of the body, he should be so constituted.
# literal_translation = Which kind of learning because to all rightly educated ought to be common, just as Aristotle concerning the study of music judged, so concerning almost all parts of liberal education it must be determined, that liberally educated, unless an art to practice he shall have decided, in none of them according to which he who that discipline professes, to excel and to surpass others he ought, but with all with a certain even measure imbued and to a certain joyful and beautiful harmony of the mind and of the body of all powers formed he may be:
# generator = deepseek-chat
