# sent_id = orat7.4.5
# text = cui rei non modo contiones et iudicia palam exercita, sed ipsa etiam theatra inservisse scimus, in quibus antiquiore saltem aetate non ut hodie magna ex parte solet, inconditae rudium et Musis invisorum ineptorumque scriptorum facetiae incultam allicientes plebem auditae sunt vel frivolae saltationes spectatae, sed summa cum arte elaborata praestantissimorum poetarum carmina.
# reading_translation = We know that not only assemblies and courts of law were openly exercised for this purpose, but even the theaters themselves served it, in which, at least in the earlier age, not as is now largely the case, were heard the unpolished jests of rude and unmusical and foolish writers, attracting the uncultivated populace, or were witnessed frivolous dances, but poems of the most excellent poets, elaborated with the highest art.
