# sent_id = orat7.5.3
# text = Nam ut in hoc utrumque aevum convenit, quod summa liberalis educationis in eo posita est, ut iuventus ad virtutem generi humano peculiarem formetur, quae cum rerum cognitione et scientia est coniunctissima, tamen illud nobis proprium, quod ab recto rerum divinarum Christo duce intellectu ingenii excolendi initium habemus.
# reading_translation = For just as in this matter both ages agree, because the highest goal of a liberal education is placed in this, that youth is formed to that virtue which is peculiar to the human race, which is most closely connected with knowledge and science of things, nevertheless that is our own special feature, that we have the beginning of cultivating the intellect from the correct understanding of divine things under Christ as leader.
