# sent_id = orat7.5.4
# text = Iam quum Christiana tum religio tum philosophia libertatem animorum postulet cum civili libertate vinculis artissimis connexam, et cuilibet servitio sit adeo infensa, ut hac fide latius propagata atque imis pectoribus infixa servitutis iugum, quo apud veteres Graecos et Romanos magna pars mortalium cum naturae humanae opprobrio oppressa iacuerat, excussum sit, licet indigna condicio a barbaris nonnullis gentibus si non plane, certe aliqua ex parte retenta, immo in novo orbe terrarum per summam impietatem et avaritiam restituta sit:
# reading_translation = Now, since the Christian religion, as well as philosophy, demands freedom of minds, which is bound by the closest ties to civil liberty, and is so hostile to every kind of servitude that, with this faith spread more widely and fixed in the depths of hearts, the yoke of slavery, under which among the ancient Greeks and Romans a great part of mortals had lain oppressed to the disgrace of human nature, has been shaken off, although the unworthy condition has been retained, if not entirely, at least in some measure, by certain barbarous nations, and indeed in the new world has been restored through the greatest impiety and avarice:
# literal_translation = Now when Christian then religion then philosophy freedom of-minds demands with civil liberty bonds closest connected, and to-every servitude is so hostile, that with-this faith more-widely spread and in-deepest breasts fixed slavery's yoke, under which among ancient Greeks and Romans great part of mortals with of-human-nature disgrace oppressed had-lain, shaken-off has-been, although unworthy condition by-barbarian some nations if not plainly, certainly in-some part retained, indeed in new world through greatest impiety and avarice restored has-been:
# generator = deepseek-chat
