# sent_id = orat7.5.60
# text = Quibus quod non omnes, qui antiquis litteris operam dant, ita ut par est commoventur, atque ad illa mores suos formant et componunt, partim in certorum quorundam ingeniorum innata et insanabili perversitate causa quaerenda est, partim in eo, quod ratione non liberali utuntur, sed vel ad quaestum faciendum vel ad famam doctrina et acumine comparandam re praestantissima abutuntur, aut quod minuta quaedam et exilia huius disciplinae frustula decerpunt, aut omnino non ut homines, sed ut animalia condocefacta nullo animi affectu non nisi sollertiam aliquam sibi compararunt, nec quid agant considerant, quid didicerint perspiciunt.
# reading_translation = The reason why not all who devote themselves to ancient literature are moved by these things as they should be, and shape and conform their characters to them, is to be sought partly in the innate and incurable perversity of certain particular minds, partly in the fact that they do not use a liberal method, but either abuse a most excellent thing for the sake of making money or gaining a reputation for learning and acumen, or because they pluck out certain minute and trivial scraps of this discipline, or, in general, not like human beings but like trained animals, with no emotional involvement, they have acquired for themselves only some skill, and do not consider what they are doing, nor perceive what they have learned.
# literal_translation = For which things that not all, who to ancient letters work give, so as is fitting are moved, and to those their characters they shape and compose, partly in of certain of some minds innate and incurable perversity cause to-be-sought is, partly in that, that method not liberal they use, but either for profit making or for fame by learning and acumen acquiring a thing most excellent they abuse, or because minute certain and trivial of this discipline scraps they pluck, or altogether not as men, but as animals trained with no of mind emotion not unless some skill for themselves they have acquired, nor what they do they consider, what they have learned they perceive.
# generator = deepseek-v4-pro
