# sent_id = orat7.6.3
# text = Nempe in hoc omnes, opinor, convenient, hodie non minus quam apud veteres corporis robur, agilitatem, celeritatem, postremo valetudinis prosperitatem maxime curandam esse, quod corpus ipsum tum sine his virtutibus multa minus commode aget, tum mentem, quam vel firmum corpus cupidinum inde manantium vi perturbat, imbecillitate etiam magis onerabit, nisi quis, quod paucorum est hominum neque omnino commendabile, corpori ita imperitare didicerit, ut id non tam subactum quam enectum teneat:
# reading_translation = Indeed, I think all will agree on this point: that today no less than among the ancients, bodily strength, agility, swiftness, and finally the flourishing of health must be especially cultivated, because the body itself, without these virtues, will both perform many things less conveniently, and will burden the mind, which even a strong body disturbs with the force of desires arising from it, even more by its weakness, unless someone, which is the case of few men and not altogether commendable, has learned to rule the body so imperiously that he keeps it not so much trained as exhausted.
# literal_translation = Indeed in this all, I think, will agree, today not less than among the ancients bodily strength, agility, swiftness, finally the prosperity of health most greatly to be cared for to be, because the body itself then without these virtues many things less conveniently will do, then the mind, which even a strong body with the force of desires from it arising disturbs, by weakness even more will burden, unless someone, which is of few men and not altogether commendable, over the body so to rule has learned, that it not so much trained as exhausted he keeps:
# generator = deepseek-chat
