# text = In Friderici Guilelmi sollemnibus nataliciis orator quotannis constitutus, auditores, non id mihi munus iniunctum unice arbitror, ut Regis dilectissimi laudes haud semel a me expositas perpetuo et de industria celebrem, qui principum gloriam minus in aequalium assentatione et praedicatione repositam videam, quam in rerum gestarum memoria ad posteros propagata et in prudentium post aliquot aetates iudicio et existimatione;
# reading_translation = Having been appointed as the orator for the annual birthday celebrations of Frederick William, listeners, I do not think that this task has been assigned to me solely for the purpose of continually and deliberately celebrating the praises of the most beloved King, which I have already set forth more than once, since I see that the glory of princes lies less in the flattery and proclamation of contemporaries than in the memory of deeds handed down to posterity and in the judgment and estimation of the wise after several generations.
# literal_translation = In the solemn birthday celebrations of Frederick William, the orator appointed annually, listeners, I do not think that this task has been enjoined on me solely, that I should celebrate perpetually and deliberately the praises of the most beloved King, which have been set forth by me more than once, who see that the glory of princes is placed less in the flattery and proclamation of contemporaries than in the memory of deeds propagated to posterity and in the judgment and estimation of the wise after several ages;
