# sent_id = orat8.2.1
# text = Sed materiam amplissimam, ex qua, quod nihil ad nos magis pertinet, capita quaedam iam olim decerpsi, quum integram ac pro argumenti et dignitate et ubertate tractare in his temporis mihi concessi angustiis nequeam, omissis ceteris locis in hoc uno nunc consistam, de quo minime omnibus constare videtur, utrum quod nonnulli contendunt, universitates litterariae eo consilio conditae condendaeve sint, ut futuri rei publicae magistratus et ministri formentur, atque universa doctoris academici disciplina huic sit fini accommodanda, an illae non ad hunc civitatis usum, sed liberaliore aliqua ratione ad propagandam litterarum doctrinam factae et institutae sint:
# reading_translation = But since I cannot treat the whole subject, which is most important and, because nothing concerns us more, I long ago selected certain topics from it, in a manner worthy of the dignity and richness of the argument within the narrow limits of time granted to me, I shall now, passing over the other points, dwell on this one alone, about which there seems to be the least agreement among all: whether, as some contend, universities have been founded or should be founded with the purpose that future magistrates and ministers of the state be formed, and the entire discipline of an academic teacher should be adapted to this end, or whether they have been established and instituted not for this practical use of the state, but on some more liberal principle for the propagation of literary learning.
# literal_translation = But the most ample material, from which, because nothing to us more pertains, certain topics already long ago I plucked, when the whole and in a manner worthy of the argument's both dignity and richness to treat in these of time to me granted narrow limits I am unable, having omitted the other points on this one now I will dwell, about which least to all to be agreed it seems, whether what some contend, universities by that plan founded or to be founded are, that future of the state magistrates and ministers be formed, and the whole of an academic teacher discipline to this end should be adapted, or those not to this of the state use, but by some more liberal principle for propagating of letters learning have been made and instituted:
# generator = deepseek-v4-pro
