# sent_id = orat8.7.1
# text = Primum genus scholas, quas populares vocant, complectitur, in quibus infantilis et puerilis aetas primis litterarum elementis, quae unicuique homini ad usum vitae maxime necessaria sunt, item fidei Christianae et morum praeceptis, decerptisque ex orbe doctrinarum minutissimis quibusdam particulis iis, quas et neminem ignorare deceat et capere vel teneri vel inculti animi possint, imbuatur, et quasi lacte communium notionum alatur:
# reading_translation = The first kind includes the schools that are called popular, in which the infantile and childish age is imbued with the first elements of letters, which are most necessary for every person for the use of life, and likewise with the precepts of the Christian faith and of morals, and with certain very small particles plucked from the circle of learning, which it is fitting that no one should be ignorant of, and which even tender or uncultivated minds can grasp, and is nourished, as it were, with the milk of common notions:
# literal_translation = The first kind the schools, which popular they call, embraces, in which the infantile and childish age with the first elements of letters, which to each person for the use of life most necessary are, likewise with the faith Christian and of morals precepts, and with plucked from the circle of learning very small certain particles those, which both no one to be ignorant of it befits and to grasp either tender or uncultivated minds can, may be imbued, and as with milk of common notions may be nourished:
