# sent_id = orat9.2.8
# text = Quod quum perficeret, si plura videtur admisisse, quae probari nequeant, cogitandum est eam fuisse rerum condicionem, ut acerbiora multa non sua sponte, sed invitus facere debuerit, quod perpetuis fere discordiis et Graecia universa et singulae civitates vexarentur, et Lacedaemoniorum potissimum, Atheniensibus ut plurimum infensorum, potentia esset reprimenda, qui principatus aeque atque Athenienses cupidi, tamen eidem retinendo impares erant.
# reading_translation = But when he accomplished this, if he seems to have admitted many things that cannot be approved, one must consider that the state of affairs was such that he had to do many harsher things not of his own accord, but unwillingly, because nearly all of Greece and the individual states were troubled by constant discord, and the power of the Lacedaemonians, who were particularly hostile to the Athenians, had to be restrained, since they, though as desirous of supremacy as the Athenians, were nevertheless unequal to maintaining it.
# literal_translation = Which when he was accomplishing, if he seems to have admitted more things, which cannot be approved, it must be thought that the condition of affairs was such, that harsher many things not of his own accord, but unwillingly he had to do, because by perpetual almost discords both all Greece and individual states were harassed, and the power of the Lacedaemonians especially, to the Athenians as mostly hostile, had to be repressed, who desirous of supremacy equally as the Athenians, nevertheless to maintaining the same were unequal.
