# sent_id = orat9.2.16
# text = At quum vel solis prudentibus in re publica regenda consiliis rebusque fortiter gestis, quibus Athenienses super ceteras Graeciae gentes cunctas extulit, magnum apud posteros meruerit nomen, tamen dubites, utrum ille patriae tantam voluerit potentiam comparare, ut artes litteraeque et cultus humanitatis universus foveri munificentius et efflorescere laetius possent, an his ipsis studuerit insignius, ut Athenarum laudem et splendorem augeret.
# reading_translation = But although he earned a great name among posterity either by the counsels of the wise alone in governing the state and by deeds bravely done, by which he raised the Athenians above all the other peoples of Greece, nevertheless you might doubt whether he wished to acquire for his fatherland so great power that arts and letters and the whole culture of humanity could be more generously fostered and flourish more joyfully, or whether he strove for these very things more notably, in order to increase the glory and splendor of Athens.
# literal_translation = But when either by the counsels of the wise alone in the state governing and by things bravely done, by which he the Athenians above the other peoples of Greece all raised, great among posterity he earned a name, nevertheless you might doubt, whether he for the fatherland so great power wished to acquire, that arts and letters and the culture of humanity whole could be fostered more generously and flourish more joyfully, or whether for these very things he strove more notably, that the glory and splendor of Athens he might increase.
# generator = deepseek-chat
