# sent_id = orat9.3.15
# text = qui quum et rerum civilium peritissimus tantaque in re publica auctoritate fuerit, ut testarum suffragiis patria expelleretur, et musicen non manu tantum et voce exercuerit, sed philosophis et mathematicis rationibus numerorum modorumque vim et potestatem sit complexus, probabile est Periclem illum tam in civitatis rebus quam in carminibus musicisque et poetis iudicandis adiutorem et amicum consiliarium habuisse.
# reading_translation = Since he was both most skilled in civil affairs and held such great authority in the state that he was banished from his country by the votes of ostracism, and since he practiced music not only with his hand and voice, but also embraced the force and power of numbers and modes with philosophical and mathematical reasoning, it is probable that that Pericles had him as an assistant and friend and counselor both in the affairs of the state and in judging poems, music, and poets.
# literal_translation = Who since and of civil affairs most-skilled and so-great in the republic authority was, that by votes of-ostracism from-country was-expelled, and music not by-hand only and by-voice exercised, but by-philosophical and by-mathematical reasonings of-numbers and-of-modes the-force and power was-comprehended, probable is Pericles that-one as in of-the-state affairs so in poems and-musics and poets judging assistant and friend counselor to-have-had.
