# sent_id = orat9.3.16
# text = Quidquid autem ad aedificia exstruenda ornandaque et ad sculpturam affinesque artes pertinebat, in eo nemo nescit Phidiam, immortalem virum, qui deorum maiestatem simulacris ab ipso confectis non assecutus est sed auxit, Pericli affuisse non solum monitorem sed etiam operum curatorem.
# reading_translation = But whatever pertained to building and adorning edifices and to sculpture and related arts, in that no one is ignorant that Phidias, an immortal man, who did not merely attain but enhanced the majesty of the gods through the statues fashioned by himself, was not only an adviser to Pericles but also a supervisor of the works.
