# sent_id = orat9.4.3
# text = non quod res publica Pericle suadente alendis omnibus sumptum impenderit, sed quod lauta et splendida civitatis administratio insignisque libertas litteris concessa honosque bonis artibus habitus praeclara ingenia prae aliis locis invitavit, et quod Atheniensium mentes ad optimum quodque studium ita erectae sunt, ut apud hos audiri, spectari, probari cultissimus quisque cuperet.
# reading_translation = Not because the state, with Pericles urging, spent money on maintaining everyone, but because the elegant and splendid administration of the city and the remarkable freedom granted to literature and the honor paid to the good arts invited outstanding talents more than other places, and because the minds of the Athenians were so raised to every best pursuit that at their city every most cultivated person wished to be heard, seen, and approved.
