# reading_translation = For after it had been sufficiently provided for the collection of wealth and the filling of the treasury, Pericles did not want the Athenian people to lie in wait for riches as if greedy, nor that gold and silver should be hidden away in the treasury, but he decided that as much as could be spent without public loss should be expended, so that the city and the temples of the gods might be magnificently adorned, and that part of the common people which would not spurn labor might be supported by an honorable livelihood:
# literal_translation = For after sufficiently it-had-been-provided for-wealth to-be-collected and for-treasury to-be-filled, Pericles the-Athenian people not as greedy to-lie-in-wait-for riches, nor gold and-silver in-the-treasury hidden to-be did-he-want, but as-much-as without public loss it-could, to-be-expended he-decided, so-that the-city and temples of-the-gods magnificently might-be-adorned, and that part of-the-people which labor not would-spurn, by-honorable might-be-supported livelihood:
