# text = fere ut Aristarchus, grammaticorum parens, interrogatus ut videtur, cur non ipse carmen componeret, quum carminum vitia et virtutes optime cognitas haberet, fertur respondisse, neque se posse scribere, quemadmodum vellet, neque velle, quemadmodum posset.
# reading_translation = Almost like Aristarchus, the father of grammarians, who, as it seems, when asked why he did not himself compose a poem, since he had the best knowledge of the faults and virtues of poems, is said to have replied that he could not write as he wished, and did not wish to write as he could.
