# sent_id = orat10.3.1
# text = Quae quum ita sint, mitto eximium illum titulum litteris nostris impositum, et in eam, unde propagatus est, aetatem relego, qua Europae nationes ex barbariae inveteratae sordibus emergentes et in veterum auctorum contemplatione incalescentes hinc omnis melioris cultus semina petebant, qua summus poeta Dantes Aligherius Virgilium tamquam omnibus numeris absolutum artis suae specimen suspiciebat, Franciscus Petrarca de restituenda in communem usum Latina lingua cogitabat, qua in Platonis et Aristotelis libris unici sanioris philosophiae fontes scaturiebant;
# reading_translation = Since these things are so, I pass over that distinguished title imposed on our literature, and I refer it back to the age from which it was propagated, in which the European nations, emerging from the filth of inveterate barbarism and growing warm in the contemplation of the ancient authors, sought from there the seeds of all better culture, in which the great poet Dante Alighieri looked up to Virgil as a specimen of his art complete in all respects, Francesco Petrarca was thinking about restoring the Latin language to common use, in which in the books of Plato and Aristotle the only sources of sounder philosophy gushed forth;
# literal_translation = Which since they are so, I send away the distinguished that title to our literature imposed, and into that, from which it is propagated, age I refer back, in which the European nations from the filth of inveterate barbarism emerging and in the contemplation of the ancient authors growing warm hence all of better culture seeds sought, in which the highest poet Dante Alighieri Virgil as in all numbers complete of his art specimen looked up to, Franciscus Petrarca about restoring into common use the Latin language was thinking, in which in the books of Plato and Aristotle the only of sounder philosophy sources gushed forth;
# generator = deepseek-chat
