# sent_id = orat10.3.13
# text = Iam ne in hac re sane magna, quod universae doctrinae caput dixerim, diutius immorer, ubi ad singulas partes perveneris, uniuscuiusque non modo bene digesta et idoneis testibus comprobata, sed summis illis notionibus congrua expositio reddenda est, ut, dum quaeque ante oculos panditur, non fortuito, sed interiore necessitate, quantum haec in rebus humanis inesse potest, ita conformatam et has decursu temporum vicissitudines expertam esse intelligamus.
# reading_translation = Now, to avoid lingering too long on this matter, which is indeed great, and which I would call the head of all learning, when you have come to the individual parts, an exposition of each one must be presented not only well arranged and confirmed by suitable witnesses, but also consistent with those highest notions, so that, while each thing is spread before our eyes, we may understand that it has been shaped not by chance but by inner necessity, as much as this can exist in human affairs, and that it has undergone these changes in the course of time.
