# sent_id = orat11.1.6
# text = haec, inquam, quum ita essent, sic tum dixit, ut quidquid a Friderico Guilelmo per tot lustra domi militiaeque egregie gestum est, quidquid prudens, pium, civile, generosum, copiose exponeret, denique Principem per omnes publicae et privatae vitae partes eximie dilaudaret, sibique, venia sit dicenti, quam successoribus benignior omnem materiam quantumvis largam secundario oratori apud memores aures praeriperet.
# reading_translation = These things, I say, since they were so, he then spoke in such a way that he would expound at length whatever had been excellently done by Frederick William through so many five-year periods at home and in war, whatever was prudent, pious, civil, generous, and finally would praise the Prince exceedingly through all parts of public and private life, and, with pardon for saying so, would snatch away from himself, or rather from his successors, all material, however ample, before a secondary orator in the presence of mindful ears.
# literal_translation = These things, I say, since they were so, thus then he spoke, that whatever by Frederick William through so many five-year periods at home and in war excellently was done, whatever prudent, pious, civil, generous, at length he would expound, finally the Prince through all parts of public and private life exceedingly he would praise, and to himself, pardon be to the one saying, than to successors more favorable all material however ample for a secondary orator before mindful ears he would snatch away.
# generator = deepseek-chat
