# sent_id = orat11.3.9
# text = Nam in iis disciplinis, quas nosse omnibus pretium est, qui rerum divinarum et humanarum notitiam a se non alienam putent, in philosophia praesertim historiaque rerumque civilium doctrina, postremo in theologorum scientia pro saeculorum ingenio alio tempore alia quum vulgo tum potentibus placent;
# reading_translation = For in those disciplines which it is valuable for everyone to know, for those who think that the knowledge of things divine and human is not foreign to them, especially in philosophy and history and the teaching of civil affairs, and finally in the science of theologians, according to the character of the ages, at one time one thing, at another another, pleases both the common people and the powerful;
# literal_translation = For in those disciplines, which to-know for-all is-a-value, who of-things divine and human knowledge from themselves not foreign may-think, in philosophy especially and-in history and-in of-civil-affairs teaching, finally in of-theologians science according-to of-ages character at-another time another-thing both to-the-common-people and to-the-powerful pleases;
