# sent_id = orat11.7.2
# text = qui si in litteris consueverint unice id, quod verum et rectum est, spectare et admirari, animumque a pravis cupidinibus, quae mortales transversos agunt, continere, etiam in ceteris vitae generibus ac negotiis et in ipsa civitate tales sese praebebunt, quales esse Fridericus Guilelmus postulat, morumque castitate, obedientia legum, fide, pietate praestabunt, et easdem artes per rem publicam universam latius latiusque disseminabunt.
# reading_translation = If they have become accustomed in their studies to look exclusively at what is true and right and to admire it, and to restrain their minds from the base desires that drive mortals astray, then even in the other walks of life and in business and in the state itself they will show themselves such as Frederick William demands, and they will excel in purity of morals, obedience to the laws, loyalty, and piety, and they will spread those same arts more and more widely throughout the whole commonwealth.
# literal_translation = Who if in letters they-have-become-accustomed solely that, which true and right is, to-look-at and to-admire, and mind from base desires, which mortals astray drive, to-restrain, even in other of-life kinds and in-businesses and in the-very state such themselves they-will-show, as to-be Frederick William demands, and of-morals by-purity, by-obedience of-laws, by-loyalty, by-piety they-will-excel, and the-same arts through the-commonwealth whole more-widely more-widely they-will-spread.
