# sent_id = orat12.1.1
# text = Friderici Guilelmi, Regis optimi, natalicia hoc anno celebraturus, auditores, non mihi videor ex ulla re gravius exordium petere posse, quam ex illius diei memoria, quo filio Regis imperii heredi et coniugi augustae connubium felix, faustum, prosperum universa civitas summis studiis apprecata est, et regiae sponsae introitum non solum tanto apparatu, quantum nos quidem in hac urbe antea non videramus, verum etiam eo animorum ardore insignem reddidit, qui certissimum praeberet intimi affectus documentum.
# reading_translation = About to celebrate the birthday of Frederick William, the best of kings, this year, listeners, I do not think I can seek a more serious beginning from any matter than from the memory of that day on which the whole state, with the greatest zeal, prayed for a happy, fortunate, and prosperous marriage for the king's son, heir to the empire, and for the august wife, and rendered the entrance of the royal bride distinguished not only by such great splendor, which indeed we had not seen before in this city, but also by that ardor of minds which would provide the surest proof of inner affection.
# literal_translation = Of Frederick William, of the best king, the birthday this year about-to-celebrate, listeners, not to-me I-seem from any matter more-gravely a-beginning to-be-able to-seek, than from the memory of that day, on which to the son of-the-king heir of-the-empire and to-the-wife august a-marriage happy, fortunate, prosperous the-whole state with-greatest zeal prayed-for, and the royal bride's entrance not only with-such great-splendor, which indeed we in this city before not had-seen, but also with-that ardor of-minds distinguished rendered, which most-certain would-provide of-inner affection a-proof.
# generator = deepseek-chat
