# text = quippe ea est dominantium in summa fortuna infelicitas, ut reperiantur qui, quo illis propiores aut sint aut esse cupiant, eo soleant minus sinceri, minus simplices et aperti esse, quin etiam eo intentius omnia et dicere et facere, quibus sibi illorum gratiam vel conservent vel comparent, privatae utilitatis causa servile obsequium simulatione voluntatis obtegentes:
# reading_translation = Indeed, such is the unhappiness of those who rule in the highest fortune, that there are found people who, the closer they are to them or wish to be, the less sincere, less simple and open they tend to be; moreover, the more intently they say and do everything by which they either preserve or acquire their favor for themselves, concealing servile obedience under the pretense of goodwill for the sake of private advantage.
# literal_translation = Indeed it is the unhappiness of the ruling ones in highest fortune, that there are found who, by how much nearer to them they either are or desire to be, by so much they are accustomed to be less sincere, less simple and open, and even the more intently all things both to say and to do, by which for themselves their favor either they preserve or acquire, for the cause of private utility servile obedience with the pretense of will concealing:
