# sent_id = orat12.5.5
# text = quum eorum, qui notiones puras cognoscere summa vi contendunt, alii haud raro in id vitium incurrant, ut vacuorum locorum designationem sterilem vel formulas inanes pro ipsa scientia et habeant et venditent, immo his ipsis sufflati sese longe sapientissimos arbitrentur, alii nimium dividendo et distinguendo cognitionis elementa ita dissecent et concidant, ut nec succus nec sanguis, sed exilis quaedam doctrinae species et umbra vix ossibus haerens relinquatur.
# reading_translation = Since, among those who strive with the greatest force to know pure concepts, some not infrequently fall into this fault, that they both hold and peddle the barren designation of empty places or empty formulas as the science itself, and indeed, puffed up with these very things, consider themselves far the wisest; while others, by excessive dividing and distinguishing, so dissect and cut up the elements of knowledge that neither juice nor blood remains, but a certain thin appearance and shadow of learning, scarcely clinging to the bones.
# literal_translation = Since of those who pure concepts to-know with-greatest force strive, some not rarely into this fault fall, that of-empty-places designation barren or formulas empty for the science itself both hold and peddle, indeed with-these-very-things puffed-up themselves far wisest consider, others by-excessively dividing and distinguishing of-knowledge elements so dissect and cut-up, that neither juice nor blood, but thin certain of-learning appearance and shadow scarcely to-bones clinging is-left.
