# text = Denique quantum creverit publica huius generis universi cura, vel hinc intelligitur, quod id a ceteris interioris rei publicae negotiis separatum et peculiari administratione dignum visum est, viris et optimis et peritissimis demandata, ac si ex summi regiminis distributione iudicare licet, eandem sibi gravitatem vindicavit, quae redituum et vectigalium universorum militariumque rerum et externarum habetur.
# reading_translation = Finally, how much the public care for this entire class of things has grown can be understood even from this, that it seemed to be separated from the other affairs of the internal state and worthy of a special administration, entrusted to the best and most experienced men, and if one may judge from the distribution of the supreme government, it claimed for itself the same importance that is held for all revenues and taxes and military and foreign affairs.
