# reading_translation = Indeed, how uncertain, how subject to the passions of men, especially amid great upheavals, this whole divination concerning the character of the present age is, not unlike the Etruscan art, seems to me to be better demonstrated by no example than by that of the greatest historian among the Germans, who for some time even lived in this city, and was distinguished among few for the elegance of his learning, the immense abundance of his erudition, and the candor of his mind.
