# sent_id = orat14.2.38
# text = Quis vero non hoc pulcherrime a medicis et medicorum alumnis institui intelligit, quod artis suae origines a remotissima aetate rimantur, quod non ea tantum, quae heri et nudius tertius proposita vel inventa sunt, suis curis digna censent, sed in singulorum morborum pertractatione docta per omnium aetatum spatia usque ad artis suae parentem Hippocratem ratione prorsus historica redeuntes, inde quidquid vel utile vel memorabile est repetunt strenue?
# reading_translation = But who does not understand that this is most beautifully established by physicians and their students, that they investigate the origins of their art from the most remote age, that they do not deem worthy of their care only those things which were proposed or invented yesterday and the day before, but in the treatment of individual diseases, returning with a truly historical method through the spaces of all ages up to Hippocrates, the father of their art, they diligently repeat from there whatever is either useful or memorable?
# literal_translation = Who but not this most beautifully by physicians and of physicians students to-be-established understands, that of art its origins from most-remote age they-search-out, that not those only, which yesterday and day-before-yesterday proposed or invented are, by their cares worthy they-judge, but in of-individual diseases treatment learned through of-all ages spaces up to of-art its parent Hippocrates with-reason truly historical returning, from-there whatever either useful or memorable is they-repeat strenuously?
