# text = Hoc ego tantum abest ut mihi persuadeam, qui praesertim non videam homines Graecam Latinamque grammaticam imprimis tenentes ceteris mortalibus animo bene conformato longe praestare, ut quamvis mentibus formandis idonea materia sit, expellendas ex scholis antiquas litteras censeam, et ingenia puerorum et adolescentium, veterum ipsorum exemplo in aliis rebus, quae nobis propiores sint, exercenda, nisi potior causa supersit, quamobrem illae deligantur.
# reading_translation = I am so far from being persuaded of this, especially since I do not see that men who especially hold Greek and Latin grammar far surpass other mortals in a well-formed mind, that although it is suitable material for forming minds, I would think that ancient literature should be expelled from schools, and that the talents of boys and adolescents should be exercised, following the example of the ancients themselves, in other things that are closer to us, unless a more important reason remains for which those [ancient letters] are chosen.
