# sent_id = orat14.3.2
# text = Intelligitis autem, auditores, dum singula eius argumenti capita, quod mihi tractandum sumpseram, strictim percurro, me in unoquoque fere ad ea digitum intendisse, quibus nostra civitas Regis sapientissimi voluntate gubernata hoc potissimum anno egregie instructa est, ut pro virium mearum modulo, exili quidem oratione sed sincera, prudentia de studiis litterarum regendis decreta continuo quodam filo quasi in corolla connecterem.
# reading_translation = You understand, listeners, that while I briefly run through the individual heads of that argument which I had undertaken to treat, I have in almost every one pointed my finger at those things with which our state, governed by the will of the wisest king, has been especially furnished in this very year, so that, according to the measure of my powers, with a speech indeed meager but sincere, I might connect in a certain continuous thread, as it were in a garland, the prudent decrees concerning the direction of literary studies.
# literal_translation = You-understand however, listeners, while the-individual heads of-that argument which I-had-undertaken to-be-treated by-me briefly I-run-through, me in almost-each-one to-those-things the-finger to-have-pointed, with-which our state of-the-king wisest by-the-will governed this very-year especially has-been-furnished, so-that according-to the-measure of-my-powers, with-meager indeed speech but sincere, the-prudent concerning-the-direction of-literary-studies decrees with-a-certain thread as-if in-a-garland I-might-connect.
