# sent_id = orat14.3.14
# text = Quod officium sanctissimum et docentibus et discentibus debet perpetuo ante oculos versari, ne in litteris unquam, vel lucro vel ambitione ducti, quidquam aliter ac salva conscientia statuant, neve sententias suas, ut eo revertar unde orsus sum, mobili saeculi ingenio, cupiditatibus hominum certo quodam tempore grassantibus, denique transiturae alicui intemperiei, quae ut in aëre et caelo, ita in humana vita cernitur, accommodent.
# reading_translation = This most sacred duty ought to be constantly kept before the eyes both of teachers and of learners, so that they never, led by profit or ambition, decide anything in literature contrary to a good conscience, and so that they do not adapt their opinions—to return to the point from which I started—to the changeable spirit of the age, to the passions of men that rage at a certain time, and finally to some passing intemperance, which is observed in the air and sky as well as in human life.
# literal_translation = Which duty most-sacred both to-teachers and to-learners ought perpetually before eyes to-be-kept, that not in literature ever, or by-profit or by-ambition led, anything otherwise than with-sound conscience they-decide, and-not their opinions, as to-that I-may-return whence I-have-begun, to-the-changeable of-the-age spirit, to-the-passions of-men at-a-certain time raging, finally to-some-passing intemperance, which as in air and sky, so in human life is-seen, they-adapt.
# generator = deepseek-chat
