# text = Sane me possem adversus haec Nicolai Machiavelli tutari verbis, qui in Principis sui, ingeniosissimi libri, dedicatione ad Laurentium Medicem scripta contendit, quemadmodum regiones delineaturi ad montium et editorum locorum naturam considerandam in planitie aliqua solent consistere, ut vero humilia et depressa cognoscant, in montibus collocantur, ita quo melius perspicias ingenium populorum, principem, quo principum rationem calleas, popularem te esse debere.
# reading_translation = Indeed, I could defend myself against these words of Niccolò Machiavelli, who in the dedication of his Prince, a most ingenious book, written to Lorenzo de' Medici, contends that just as those who are about to map out regions are accustomed to stand on some plain in order to consider the nature of mountains and elevated places, but in order to recognize low and depressed places they are placed on mountains, so, in order that you may better perceive the character of peoples, you ought to be a prince, and in order that you may understand the reasoning of princes, you ought to be a popular man.
# literal_translation = Indeed I could defend myself against these words of Nicolaus Machiavelli, who in the dedication of his Prince, a most ingenious book, written to Laurentius Medices contends, that just as those about to delineate regions are accustomed to stand on some plain for the sake of considering the nature of mountains and elevated places, but in order that they may recognize low and depressed things, they are placed on mountains, so in order that you may better perceive the character of peoples, a prince, in order that you may understand the reasoning of princes, a popular man you ought to be.
