# sent_id = orat15.2.17
# text = At istius excusationi, quae ambitiosior est quam pro mea mediocritate, praeferenda videtur haec paullo modestior, non me profunda disputatione et digna homine rem publicam experto, a qua meo iure absum, qualem principem esse oporteat, explicaturum, sed populari via, ut qui, cur optimo Regi tantopere obstrictus sit populus, exponere nunc constituerim;
# reading_translation = But to that excuse of his, which is more ambitious than befits my mediocrity, this somewhat more modest one seems preferable: that I shall not explain, by a profound discussion worthy of a man experienced in public affairs (from which I am rightly absent), what sort of prince one ought to be, but rather in a popular manner, as one who has now decided to set forth why the people are so greatly bound to the best King.
# literal_translation = But to that excuse of his, which is more ambitious than for my mediocrity, to be preferred seems this somewhat more modest, not me by profound discussion and worthy of a man having experienced the republic, from which by my right I am absent, what sort of prince it is fitting to be, about to explain, but by popular way, as who, why to the best King so greatly bound is the people, to set forth now I may have decided;
