# sent_id = orat15.3.1
# text = Equidem regiam definiturus virtutem non recitabo vobis indicem omnium ingenii dotium, quae ut in aliis bonis viris, ita in principibus inesse debeant, sed duplici eam dico animi indole contineri, strenua fortitudine et miti sapientia, quae etiamsi possunt inter se contrariae videri, tamen in viro bono prorsus conspirant.
# reading_translation = Indeed, intending to define royal virtue, I will not recite to you a list of all the gifts of talent, which, as they ought to be in other good men, so they ought to be in princes, but I say that it is contained in a twofold character of mind: vigorous courage and gentle wisdom, which, even if they can seem contrary to each other, nevertheless in a good man entirely conspire.
