# sent_id = orat16.1.1
# text = Quum permultae causae sint, auditores, quamobrem Friderici Guilelmi natalicia tanta nos quotannis celebritate obeamus, eaeque partim rei publicae universae communes, quod optimum Principem venerari, beneficia ab illo in civitatem collata pio animo recolere, Deo Optimo Maximo pro illius salute gratias agere et identidem vota facere pariter interest omnium, partim vero nobis propriae et peculiares, quod ille scholam hanc non solum condidit, sed etiam insigniore fovet cura, atque ita diligit, ut suo eam nomine ornaverit nuperrime;
# reading_translation = Since there are very many reasons, listeners, why we celebrate the birthday of Frederick William every year with such great festivity, and these reasons are partly common to the whole state, because it is equally the interest of all to venerate the best Prince, to recall with pious mind the benefits conferred by him upon the state, to give thanks to God, the Best and Greatest, for his health, and to make vows again and again; but partly they are proper and peculiar to us, because he not only founded this school, but also fosters it with more distinguished care, and so loves it that he has recently adorned it with his own name;
# literal_translation = Since very many causes are, hearers, on-account-of-which of-Frederick-William the-birthday so-great we yearly with-celebration we-celebrate, and-these partly of-the-commonwealth whole common, because best Prince to-venerate, benefits by-him into the-state conferred with-pious mind to-recall, to-God Best Greatest for his health thanks to-give and again-and-again vows to-make equally is-of-interest of-all, partly but to-us proper and peculiar, because he this school not only founded, but also with-more-distinguished care fosters, and so loves, that with-his it name has-adorned recently;
# generator = deepseek-chat
