# sent_id = orat16.4.18
# text = Nonne, licet hoc regnum e variis gentibus fortuito quodammodo quasi elementorum concursu accreverit, vis imperii certum tenentis temperamentum, et legum atque institutorum quaedam aequalitas, cui etiam paria litterarum et artium studia annumeranda sunt, et unus qui gubernat omnes, qui omnibus aequus est, Principis dilectissimi animus, Transrhenanum et Transvistulanum, Viadrique et Albis et Visurgis accolas et interiectas provincias cunctas non armis, sed voluntatum consensu, in hoc unum nomen Borussicum consociat?
# reading_translation = Does not, although this kingdom has grown together from various peoples as if by a fortuitous concourse of elements, the power of a ruler holding a certain balance, and a certain equality of laws and institutions, to which even the equal pursuits of letters and arts are to be counted, and one who governs all, who is fair to all, the spirit of a most beloved Prince, unite the inhabitants of the Rhine and the Vistula, the Oder, the Elbe, and the Saale, and all the intervening provinces, not by arms, but by the consent of their wills, into this one Prussian name?
# literal_translation = Not, although this kingdom from various peoples fortuitously in-a-way as-if of-elements by-a-concourse has-grown, the-power of-a-ruler a-certain balance holding, and of-laws and of-institutions a-certain equality, to-which even equal of-letters and of-arts pursuits are-to-be-counted, and one who governs all, who to-all is-fair, of-a-Prince most-beloved the-spirit, Transrhenane and Transvistulane, and-of-the-Oder and-of-the-Elbe and-of-the-Saale inhabitants and intervening provinces all not by-arms, but of-wills by-consent, into this one name Prussian unites?
# generator = deepseek-chat
