# sent_id = orat16.5.12
# text = Quod siquis multiplicis illius apparatus doctrinarum eam tantum partem in civitate retinendam censuerit, quae ipsius convenire rationibus videatur, et fundamenta litterarum, abstrusa illa nec communi usui apta, labefactaverit, nec multo aliter egerit atque Cynici, qui quod ad recte vivendum hominem sibi sufficere arbitrabantur, fuste et pera ollaque et poculo, vel pro hoc etiam concava manu contenti, quidquid supellectilis et utensilium exornat vitam et iucundiorem reddit, feruntur sprevisse.
# reading_translation = But if anyone should think that only that part of that manifold apparatus of learning should be retained in the state which seems to suit his own purposes, and should undermine the foundations of literature, those hidden things and not suited to common use, and should act not much differently than the Cynics, who, because they thought that a man suffices for himself for living rightly, are said to have scorned with club and wallet and pot and cup, or even with a hollow hand instead of these, whatever of furniture and utensils adorns life and makes it more pleasant.
# literal_translation = But if anyone that manifold apparatus of learning only that part in the state to be retained should have thought, which itself to his own purposes to suit seems, and the foundations of literature, hidden those and not to common use suited, should have undermined, and not much differently should have acted than the Cynics, who because for living rightly a man to himself to suffice they thought, with club and wallet and pot and cup, or for this even with hollow hand content, whatever of furniture and of utensils adorns life and more pleasant makes, are said to have scorned.
