# sent_id = orat16.5.13
# text = Hoc unum concedendum iudico, esse quandam quasi emortuam eruditionem vel potius eruditionis speciem et imitationem, quae quantumvis sese iactet, prorsus illiberalis et umbratica neque ingenium exerceat nec iudicium acuat, nec notionibus impleat animum, neque doceat quidquam aut recreet et oblectet, sed inanes in horrea sua constipet paleas, et in solis habitans librorum voluminibus nihil mente comprehendat.
# reading_translation = I judge that this one thing must be conceded: that there is a certain, as it were, dead learning, or rather a semblance and imitation of learning, which, however much it may boast itself, is utterly illiberal and shadowy, and neither exercises the mind nor sharpens the judgment, nor fills the soul with notions, nor teaches anything or refreshes and delights, but packs empty chaff into its granaries, and dwelling among the volumes of books alone, comprehends nothing with the mind.
# literal_translation = This one thing to-be-conceded I-judge, to-be a-certain as-it-were dead learning or rather of-learning a-semblance and imitation, which however-much itself it-may-boast, utterly illiberal and shadowy and neither the-mind it-exercises nor the-judgment it-sharpens, nor with-notions it-fills the-soul, nor it-teaches anything or refreshes and delights, but empty into its granaries it-packs chaff, and in alone dwelling of-books volumes nothing with-the-mind it-comprehends.
