# sent_id = orat17.3.5
# text = sic, ut militaris exempla absolutissima, qualia nostra aetate vix nisi inter barbaros reppereris, ex antiquis petam rebus publicis, quae licet tam exiguae fuerint, ut una essent urbe vel paucarum communione circumscriptae, tamen clarissimas variarum, quas civitas induit, formarum imagines offerunt, et ob hoc ipsum, quod simpliciores fuerunt, singula civitatis elementa exhibent distinctiora;
# reading_translation = Thus, in order that I may seek from ancient republics the most perfect examples of military affairs, such as in our age you will scarcely find except among barbarians, which, although they were so small that they were confined to one city or to the communion of a few, nevertheless offer the clearest images of the various forms which the state has assumed, and for this very reason, because they were simpler, they exhibit the individual elements of the state more distinctly;
# literal_translation = Thus, so that military examples most-perfect, such-as in-our age scarcely except among barbarians you-will-have-found, from ancient republics I-may-seek, which although so small they-were, that they-were one city or of-few communion circumscribed, nevertheless most-clear of-various, which the-state has-put-on, forms images they-offer, and on-account-of this very, because simpler they-were, individual of-the-state elements they-exhibit more-distinct;
