# text = Quae quum, mea quidem sententia, eum sibi finem debeat propositum habere, ut discipulos non ad certam quandam sive negotiorum sive litterarum partem exercendam condocefaciat, sed liberali formet eruditione, aptosque reddat ei, quam quisque deinceps pro indolis ratione elegerit, disciplinae cum fructu capessendae, simul ut eos iis imbuat studiis, quae, ut ait Cicero, adolescentiam agunt, senectutem oblectant, secundas res ornant, adversis perfugium et solatium praebent:
# reading_translation = Since, in my opinion at least, it (the academic profession) ought to have set before itself the goal of training students not for the practice of some particular kind of business or literature, but of forming them with a liberal education, and of making them fit for taking up with profit that discipline which each one will have chosen in accordance with the bent of his nature; at the same time, to imbue them with those studies which, as Cicero says, accompany youth, delight old age, adorn prosperity, and offer refuge and solace in adversity:
# literal_translation = Which since, in my indeed opinion, it ought to have set before itself as a goal, that it should train students not for some particular part of business or of literature to be practiced, but should form them with liberal education, and should render them fit for that discipline, which each one afterwards according to the reason of his nature will have chosen, to be taken up with profit, at the same time that it should imbue them with those studies, which, as Cicero says, drive youth, delight old age, adorn prosperous affairs, to adverse affairs refuge and solace provide:
# generator = deepseek-chat
