# sent_id = orat18.1.1
# text = Qui dies Regem optimum et nemini non carissimum huic rei publicae dedit, Princeps regni heres serenissime, auditores omnium ordinum ornatissimi, is dies festus eodem pietatis affectu a populo universo quotannis obitur, quod Fridericus Guilelmus eadem perpetuo caritate prosequitur cives, eadem constantia rei publicae salutem tuetur et confirmat, pacem bona quaelibet dispensantem, publicas domesticasque opes, vires exercitus, florem artium et litterarum, denique communes omnium, privatas singulorum utilitates quasvis.
# reading_translation = The day that gave to this republic the best king, dear to everyone, most serene Prince, heir to the throne, most distinguished auditors of all ranks, that festive day is observed annually by the whole people with the same feeling of devotion, because Frederick William with the same perpetual affection pursues the citizens, with the same constancy protects and strengthens the welfare of the republic, peace dispensing all good things, public and domestic resources, the strength of the army, the flower of arts and letters, and finally all common advantages of all, and any private advantages of individuals.
# literal_translation = Which day the best king and to no one not most dear to this republic gave, Prince heir of the kingdom most serene, auditors of all orders most distinguished, that day festive with the same feeling of piety by the people whole annually is observed, because Frederick William with the same perpetual love pursues citizens, with the same constancy of the republic the welfare protects and strengthens, peace all good things dispensing, public and domestic resources, strength of the army, flower of arts and letters, finally common of all, private of individuals advantages any.
