# text = cuius rei uberiorem explanationem ab ipso promissam etsi nobis invidit fortuna, tamen ex eius Politicis intelligas, ex illius sententia, ut qui sacro furore agitentur, sacris item canticis usi sedantur et componuntur, medicinam et purgationem nacti, ita qui formidolosi vel misericordes, aut generatim animi perturbationibus sint obnoxii, gustatis spectando his commotionibus levari cum voluptate et purgari, iis aliqua ex parte exsolutos.
# reading_translation = Although fortune has denied us the richer explanation of this matter that he himself promised, nevertheless from his Politics you may understand, according to his opinion, that just as those who are driven by sacred frenzy, having used sacred songs, are calmed and composed, having obtained medicine and purification, so those who are prone to fear or pity, or generally to disturbances of the soul, having tasted these emotions by watching, are relieved with pleasure and purified, being to some extent released from them.
