# reading_translation = From there, besides the plaster casts, an excellent aid to studies, and other things to be preserved separately, the monuments of Egyptian antiquity have been left in a city garden situated not far away, where we see whatever that clever and industrious people fabricated for the adornment of their domestic and daily worship, as if snatched from the underworld, together with the most ancient images of the gods, not yet having been rendered with the beauty of the human form according to the Greek manner, but hard, stiff, and grim, so that they might be even more significant by their monstrosity.
