# sent_id = orat19.1.1
# text = Superiore anno, auditores, quum die laetissimo Friderici Guilelmi natali in hoc conventu verba facerem, vix dum ad nos allatus erat primus nuntius ingentis istius motus, quo, postquam Borbonici regis sive error fatalis, sive quoquo vocabulo inceptum damnosissimum nominare libuerit, urbanae multitudinis aciem inconditam in praetorianos et reliquos milites concitavit, civitas Galliarum princeps caedibus et cruore polluta, ac paucorum dierum discrimine patrio regno exuta, patrio solo pulsa ea familia est, quam aliquot lustris ante nostri et sociorum exercitus atrocissimis proeliis multoque sanguine semel atque iterum constituerant et stabiliverant.
# reading_translation = Last year, my listeners, when on the most joyful birthday of Frederick William I spoke in this assembly, the first news of that enormous upheaval had scarcely reached us, by which, after the fatal error of the Bourbon king, or whatever name one may wish to call that most ruinous undertaking, stirred up the undisciplined mass of the urban multitude against the praetorians and the remaining soldiers, the leading city of the Gauls, polluted with slaughter and blood, and within the space of a few days stripped of the ancestral kingdom, driven from the ancestral soil, that family which a few decades earlier our armies and those of the allies had established and stabilized once and again with most fierce battles and much blood.
# literal_translation = In the previous year, listeners, when on the most joyful day of Frederick William's birthday in this assembly I was making a speech, scarcely yet to us had been brought the first news of that enormous upheaval, by which, after the Bourbon king's either fatal error, or by whatever word it may please to name the most ruinous undertaking, he stirred up the undisciplined battle-line of the urban multitude against the praetorians and the remaining soldiers, the leading city of the Gauls, polluted with slaughters and blood, and by the interval of a few days from the ancestral kingdom stripped, from the ancestral soil driven out, that family is, which a few lustra before our and the allies' armies with most fierce battles and much blood once and again had established and had stabilized.
# generator = deepseek-chat
