# text = Quodsi tamen hoc rege haud immunes ingentium malorum fuimus et sumus, si bella primum adversa, mox secunda quidem sed tanto cruentiora gesta sunt, unde magna vis aeris alieni contrahenda rei publicae fuit, si in pace modo quaestus inopia et agrorum sterilitas urget, modo ipsa fertilitas et frugum copia indeque accidens vilitas annonae fundorum possessores et colonos premere, quin nonnullis etiam nimia populi frequentia, cui alendae vix sufficere agricultura, opificia, commercia queant, adducere discrimina videtur, si quum maxime belli metus et nata ex tot turbis communis animorum agitation et morbi grassantis saevitia cum caeli intemperie angunt, magnasque in exercitus et tuendos imperii limites etiam adversus amicos postulant impensas:
# reading_translation = But if nevertheless under this king we have not been and are not free from enormous evils, if wars were waged at first unsuccessfully, then indeed successfully but so much the bloodier, from which a great mass of debt had to be contracted by the state, if in peace now scarcity of profit and sterility of the fields oppress, now fertility itself and abundance of crops and the resulting cheapness of grain press upon the owners of estates and the farmers, indeed to some even the excessive population, which agriculture, manufactures, and commerce can scarcely suffice to feed, seems to bring dangers, if at the very moment fear of war and the general agitation of minds born from so many disturbances and the savagery of a raging disease together with the intemperance of the climate torment us, and demand great expenses for the armies and for guarding the boundaries of the empire even against friends:
