# sent_id = orat19.3.65
# text = Postremo vota facimus Deo Optimo Maximo, ut Fridericus Guilelmus cum universa domo Augusta florentissima servetur incolumis, ut illo duce patria nostra firmioribus et liberalioribus in dies institutis augeatur, ut nulla neque imprudentia nec pravitate rumpatur sanctissimum caritatis vinculum, ut, si fieri potest, finis imponatur stragibus, quibus atteruntur gentes, atque ut pax, artium et litterarum nutrix, bonorum omnium mater confirmetur, communisque cesset metus et reddatur securitas.
# reading_translation = Finally, we make vows to God, the Best and Greatest, that Frederick William, together with his entire August house, may be preserved safe and most flourishing; that under his leadership our fatherland may be strengthened day by day with firmer and more liberal institutions; that the most sacred bond of love may not be broken by any imprudence or wickedness; that, if possible, an end may be put to the slaughters by which nations are worn away; and that peace, the nurse of arts and letters, the mother of all good things, may be confirmed, and that common fear may cease and security be restored.
# literal_translation = Finally vows we-make to-God Best Greatest, that Frederick William with whole house August most-flourishing may-be-preserved safe, that under-him leader fatherland-our with-firmer and more-liberal in days institutions may-be-increased, that no neither imprudence nor wickedness may-be-broken most-sacred bond of-love, that, if may-be-done, end may-be-put to-slaughters, by-which are-worn-away nations, and that peace, of-arts and of-letters nurse, of-good-things all mother may-be-confirmed, and-common may-cease fear and may-be-restored security.
# generator = deepseek-chat
