# sent_id = orat20.2.171
# text = Constat Fridericum aetate provectum Graecos Latinosque auctores classicos, quorum ope restitutae doctrinae et artes erant, qui inde ab instaurato ingeniorum cultu scholasticae inserviebant institutioni, iussisse in gymnasiis diligentius atque ita potissimum tractari, ut scriptorum non solum vocabula mandarentur memoriae, sed etiam rebus, sententiis, doctrina, quae iis continetur, disserendi via et ratione, quam praeierunt insecutis saeculis, imbuerentur animi.
# reading_translation = It is well known that Frederick, when advanced in age, ordered that the classical Greek and Latin authors, by whose aid learning and the arts had been restored, and who from the revival of culture had served scholastic instruction, should be treated in the gymnasia with greater diligence and in such a way especially that not only the words of the writers should be committed to memory, but also that minds should be imbued with the matter, the sentiments, and the doctrine contained in them, and with the method and system of discourse which they had set forth for subsequent ages.
# literal_translation = It is established that Frederick, with age advanced, the Greek and Latin classical authors, by whose help restored were learning and arts, who from the renewed cultivation of talents served scholastic instruction, ordered in the gymnasia to be treated more diligently and so especially, that of the writers not only the words should be committed to memory, but also with the things, sentiments, doctrine, which in them is contained, with the way and method of discoursing, which they showed to following ages, should be imbued the minds.
# generator = deepseek-chat
