# sent_id = orat20.2.197
# text = Hanc viam ubi sequi docentibus licet, ubi praeterea universitates litterariae, quae ipsum nomen inde traxerunt, quod collegia sive corpora sunt res suas certis legibus regentia, non privantur iuribus, quae ipsis competunt, nec nimis vel iusto severius, sed moderate et benevole gubernantur ab iis, quos princeps curatores et quasi custodes addit, ibi vera mihi videtur libertas academica retineri.
# reading_translation = Where it is permitted to follow this path under the guidance of teachers, and where, moreover, universities, which derive their very name from the fact that they are associations or bodies that manage their own affairs according to fixed laws, are not deprived of the rights that belong to them, nor are they governed too strictly or more severely than is right, but are governed moderately and benevolently by those whom the prince appoints as curators and, as it were, guardians, there, in my opinion, true academic freedom is preserved.
# literal_translation = This path when to follow for-teachers it-is-permitted, where moreover universities, which the very name from-there have-drawn, because associations or bodies are things their-own by-certain-laws governing, not are-deprived of-rights, which to-themselves belong, nor too or more-than-just more-severely, but moderately and benevolently are-governed by those, whom the-prince curators and as-if guardians adds, there true to-me seems academic freedom to-be-retained.
