# text = Eandem gratiam universi et agimus et habemus Friderico Guilelmo, scholae nostrae statori et altori, qui non modo traditum a maioribus litterarum adiuvandarum studium retinet ac tuetur, sed illos longe superat munificentia et benignitate, ac per omnes provincias regni late propagati bonis artibus tam novas et florentissimas sedes condidit, quam vetustas lautius instruxit, neque institutionem publicam artioribus adstringit formulis, sed debitam tantum sacris legibusque reverentiam iniungit docentibus.
# reading_translation = We both express and feel the same gratitude to Frederick William, the founder and nourisher of our school, who not only maintains and protects the inherited zeal for supporting literature from our ancestors, but far surpasses them in generosity and kindness, and throughout all the provinces of the widely extended kingdom has established for the good arts as new and flourishing seats as antiquity furnished more splendidly, and does not confine public education to narrower formulas, but only imposes on teachers the reverence due to sacred laws.
