# sent_id = orat21.2.67
# text = Praeterea civilis disciplina ut cum sacerdotibus, ita cum iis, qui reconditiori et abstrusiori philosophiae cognitioni operam dant, incidit in dissensum, quum tamen eandem illa ratio, quam quaerunt sapientiae studiosi, etiam civitatem permeare paullo perfectiorem videatur, siquidem, quod ipsis philosophis auctoribus profitetur vir rerum publicarum haud mediocriter peritus, M.
# reading_translation = Moreover, civil discipline, just as it comes into conflict with priests, so also with those who devote themselves to the knowledge of a more recondite and abstruse philosophy, although that same reason, which the students of wisdom seek, seems to permeate the state in a somewhat more perfect way, since, as a man not moderately skilled in public affairs declares on the authority of the philosophers themselves, M.
