# reading_translation = But those civil lawyers and fierce advocates, who would laugh at a philosopher's inexperience, if someone tried to raise them to higher things, would either themselves withdraw from such a question as, "What wrong have I done to you, or you to me?" in order to inquire what justice and injustice themselves are, and how these differ from each other and from all other concepts, or if they passed from this opinion, "Happy is the king who possesses much gold," to questions about the nature of kingship and about human happiness and misery in general;
