# text = Friderici Guilelmi iudicium ita confirmavit eventus, ut, quod nec locorum amoenitas, nec vini copia, nec venia insolentiae quemquam ut huc concederet allexit, nulla pars iuventutis egerit innocentius quam nostra haec cohors, nulla insignior fuerit studiorum alacritate, industria, severitate, immo ut iam fateantur plurimi, atque imprimis rerum publicarum praesides, nihil esse utilius hac universitatum in urbibus principibus habitatione tranquillissima.
# reading_translation = The outcome has so confirmed Frederick William's judgment that, since neither the charm of the place, nor the abundance of wine, nor the indulgence of insolence enticed anyone to come here, no part of the youth has spent its time more innocently than this our band, none has been more distinguished for eagerness in study, industry, and strictness—indeed, as many now admit, and especially the governors of states—nothing is more useful than this most tranquil residence of universities in capital cities.
