# sent_id = orat22.2.26
# text = Haec est enim studiorum in Germania ratio, ut neque scholae quas vocant speciales, quarum tenuitas et languor nonnullis perplacet, neque academiae doctrinarum quamvis eruditae et splendidae, neque ulla alia instituta scholastica tantos mentibus stimulos adiiciant, tanto bonarum artium summa contentione colendarum ardore incendant iuveniles animos, quanto haec universitatum disciplina, sine qua, ut nunc quidem comparatus populorum Europae cultus est, litterae non videntur vigere et florere posse.
# reading_translation = For this is the condition of studies in Germany, that neither the so-called special schools, whose meagerness and languor please some people, nor the academies of learning, however learned and splendid, nor any other scholastic institutions add such great stimuli to minds, nor inflame youthful souls with such great ardor for cultivating the good arts with the utmost exertion, as this discipline of universities, without which, as the culture of the European peoples is now indeed constituted, letters do not seem able to thrive and flourish.
# literal_translation = This is for the condition of studies in Germany, that neither schools which they call special, whose meagerness and languor to some pleases, nor academies of learning however learned and splendid, nor any other institutions scholastic so great to minds stimuli add, so great of good arts with utmost exertion of cultivating ardor inflame youthful souls, as this of universities discipline, without which, as now indeed compared the culture of peoples European is, letters not seem to thrive and to flourish to be able.
