# text = tum, postquam calamitate faustissima accidit, ut generosam iuventutem in castra evocatam dimitteremus haud inviti, quae sese ea tempestate pro salute Regis et patriae devoverat sponte, cum populo universo libertatem nostram gloriamque Borussicam imperiique integritatem et cetera bona sanguine suo redemptura et recuperatura, non modo damnum huic scholae datum statim reparatum est, sed auctibus continuis ita mox increvit civium numerus, brevi ut reliquas universitates superaremus omnes;
# reading_translation = Then, after the most fortunate calamity happened, that we dismissed the noble youth, called to the camp, not unwillingly, who at that time had devoted themselves of their own accord for the safety of the King and the fatherland, since with the whole people they were about to redeem and recover our liberty and the Prussian glory and the integrity of the empire and other goods with their blood, not only was the damage given to this school immediately repaired, but with continuous increases the number of citizens soon grew so much that in a short time we surpassed all other universities.
