# sent_id = orat22.2.45
# text = Nec vereor adeo, ne in peritorum reprehensionem incurram magnopere, ubi paullo fortasse ambitiosius dixero in transitu, hac scholae nostrae celebritate effici, ut regni Borussici virtus magis intelligatur, dum bonae iuvenes indolis undique huc affluentes propius cognoscunt huius rei publicae bona et commoda, et quod saepe sum expertus ipse, nominis Borussici existimatione sensim imbuuntur ac trahuntur vel nolentes et quodammodo inscientes.
# reading_translation = Nor do I fear so much that I will greatly incur the censure of the learned, when perhaps I say somewhat more ambitiously in passing, that by this celebrated gathering of our school it is brought about that the virtue of the Prussian kingdom is better understood, while young men of good character, flocking here from all sides, come to know more closely the goods and advantages of this commonwealth, and, as I have often experienced myself, are gradually imbued with and drawn by the esteem of the Prussian name, even unwilling and in a way unknowing.
# literal_translation = Nor do-I-fear so-much, lest into the-censure of-the-experienced I-may-fall greatly, where perhaps more-ambitiously I-shall-have-said in passing, by-this of-our-school celebratedness it-is-brought-about, that of-the-Prussian-kingdom the-virtue more is-understood, while good of-character young-men from-everywhere here flowing-together more-closely they-come-to-know of-this commonwealth the-goods and advantages, and what often I-have-experienced myself, of-the-Prussian-name by-the-esteem gradually they-are-imbued and they-are-drawn even unwilling and in-a-way unknowing.
