# reading_translation = Moreover, from our scholastic discipline, properly tempered by laws, and from the study of antiquity, you would not more justly derive a blemish on account of the age than if someone, just as the Greeks had persuaded themselves that by learning softer and more licentious harmonies the minds of boys were rendered idle and intemperate, should in like manner derive this, as it were, intemperance of the age from our musicians, or from the theaters, in which indeed we not infrequently hear most distinguished poets, the glories of Germany, proclaiming civil liberty.
