# text = igitur si vellent iis infensi esse, qui studerent aequales suos iisdem rebus superare, quibus Athenienses superarent reliquos universos, et qui ea uterentur eruditione, cuius Athenae duces et parentes fuissent, civitatem sua semet ipsam sententia condemnaturam, atque idem facturam, ac si Lacedaemonii animadverterent in artis militaris magistros, vel Thessali in eos, qui equitandi modos docerent.
# reading_translation = Therefore, if they wished to be hostile to those who strove to surpass their contemporaries in the same things by which the Athenians surpassed all others, and who used that education of which Athens had been the leader and parent, the city would condemn itself by its own judgment, and would do the same as if the Lacedaemonians punished the teachers of the military art, or the Thessalians those who taught the methods of horsemanship.
# literal_translation = Therefore if they wished to be hostile to those who strove to surpass their equals in the same things by which the Athenians surpassed all the rest, and who used that education of which Athens had been leaders and parents, the city would condemn itself by its own judgment, and would do the same as if the Lacedaemonians should punish the teachers of the military art, or the Thessalians those who taught the modes of horsemanship.
