# sent_id = orat23.2.6
# text = et quanquam ego mihi hoc, quod ille divinaverit, vix longo ex intervallo ac per nebulam videor conspicere, atque ita fit, ut quod ipsum exiguum et obscurum sit, id mihi obtusior acies repraesentet etiam minutius et hebetius, tamen iuvat vel incondita voce, quantum fieri per temporis angustiam potest, adumbrare quale id mihi obversetur ante oculos.
# reading_translation = And although I seem to perceive, after a long interval and as if through a mist, what he has divined, and it happens that what is itself small and obscure is represented to me by my blunter vision as even smaller and duller, yet it pleases me, even with an unpolished voice, as far as can be done within the narrowness of time, to sketch out what sort of thing appears before my eyes.
