# reading_translation = Or shall we say that human affairs indeed have their prescribed changes, but just as the sky and the stars, moving in a circle perpetually, after completing their course also return to the same place from which they set out, so human affairs too, imitating the heavenly order, are driven around in a circle as if by certain whirlwinds, and after completing the circle, after so many ages, after so many and such great labors of mortals, have not advanced a step, but have been cast back to the beginning of the course, and that the human race, pierced through, performs the leaky jars of the Danaids, continually pouring in water that continually flows out?
