# sent_id = orat24.2.18
# text = Nam primum quamquam privado non modo hanc damus veniam, ut ad unam aliquam rem animum appellat potissimum, sed hoc ipsum putamus utile ac necessarium esse, propterea quod singuli singulis quibusdam rebus vel artibus tractandis et suapte natura aptiores sunt et exercitatione fiunt etiam sollertiores, dum ii, qui in nulla arte habitant et perseverant, sed huc illuc volitantes, veluti apes ex floribus, variis ex disciplinis trahere aliquid nutrimenti et carpere fructus solent, multa quidem conantur et aliqua imbuuntur incondita eruditione, sed nec perficiuntur ipsi nec quidquam fere perficiunt:
# reading_translation = For first, although we grant this indulgence not only to a private individual, that he should apply his mind especially to some one thing, but we also think this very thing useful and necessary, for the reason that individuals are both by their own nature more suited to certain particular things or arts to be practiced, and by practice become even more skillful, while those who do not dwell and persevere in any art, but flitting about here and there, like bees from flowers, are accustomed to draw some nourishment and gather fruits from various disciplines, attempt many things and are imbued with some rough learning, but neither are they perfected themselves nor do they accomplish anything at all.
# literal_translation = For first although to-a-private-individual not only this we-give indulgence, that to one some thing the-mind he-may-apply especially, but this very we-think useful and necessary to-be, for-the-reason-that individuals to-certain particular things or arts to-be-practiced both by-their-own-nature more-suited are and by-exercise become even more-skillful, while those, who in no art dwell and persevere, but here and-there flitting-about, like bees from flowers, from-various disciplines to-draw some nourishment and to-gather fruits are-accustomed, many-things indeed they-attempt and with-some rough-learning they-are-imbued, but neither are-perfected themselves nor anything almost they-accomplish:
