# sent_id = orat24.2.31
# text = tamen princeps, qui non in singulis rebus tractandis et singulari quodam officio obeundo versatur, sed tenet gubernacula, non debet ullam artem aut negotium ita habere carum, ut reliqua opinetur vel negligenda vel contemnenda, sed ut numen rerum moderans universitati cunctis providet huius mundi partibus, comprehendere omnia pari cura, omnia vitae genera pro ipsorum dignitate et gravitate acri aestimare iudicio, et sese his omnibus benignum praebere.
# reading_translation = Nevertheless, a leader, who is not engaged in handling individual matters and performing some particular duty, but holds the reins of government, ought not to hold any art or business so dear as to think that the rest are to be neglected or despised, but, just as the divine power that governs the universe provides for all parts of this world, he should embrace all things with equal care, judge all kinds of life according to their own dignity and importance with keen judgment, and show himself kind to all of them.
# literal_translation = Nevertheless, a leader, who not in individual matters handling and in a particular duty performing is engaged, but holds the reins, not ought any art or business so to have dear, that the rest he thinks either to be neglected or to be despised, but as the divine power of things moderating to the whole universe provides for all parts of this world, to comprehend all things with equal care, all kinds of life according to their own dignity and gravity with keen judgment to estimate, and himself to all these kind to show.
# generator = deepseek-chat
