# sent_id = orat24.2.76
# text = Tantum enim abest, ut hac re caveantur delicta, quae dum committit, nemo fere legum et animadversionum memor est, sed ira et odio et vesanis ducitur cupiditatibus, vel sperat se effugere poenam et latere vindicem posse, ut etiam provocari maleficia animadversione saeva videantur, quod improbi et audaces homines exemplo civitatis instituuntur ad crudelitatem.
# reading_translation = For it is so far from being the case that crimes are prevented by this means, that while a person commits them, hardly anyone is mindful of the laws and punishments, but is driven by anger and hatred and mad desires, or hopes that he can escape punishment and hide from the avenger, that even wrongdoings seem to be provoked by cruel punishment, because wicked and bold men are trained to cruelty by the example of the state.
# literal_translation = So far indeed it is absent, that by this thing crimes are guarded against, which while he commits, no one almost of laws and punishments is mindful, but by anger and hatred and mad is led desires, or hopes himself to escape punishment and to lie hidden avenger able, that even provoked wrongdoings by punishment cruel seem, because wicked and bold men by example of state are trained to cruelty.
