# text = Quod munus mihi demandatum est, auditores, hoc die faustissimo, quem Friderici Guilelmi nomini colendo civium pietas dedicavit publice et consecravit, ex loco hoc amplissimo dicendi, quamquam cum plerisque intelligo, ut honorificum illustrissimo cuique et mihi iucundum, ita propter rei dignitatem esse imprimis grave, argumentique gravitati magis responsuram orationem, ubi non ego solus hac splendida augear praerogativa, sed per vices alius quotannis alii orator succedat:
# reading_translation = The task entrusted to me, listeners, on this most auspicious day, which the piety of the citizens has publicly dedicated and consecrated to the honoring of the name of Frederick William, from this most distinguished place of speaking, although I understand with most people that it is as honorable to every most distinguished man and pleasant to me, so on account of the dignity of the matter it is especially serious, and that an oration would better correspond to the gravity of the subject, where not I alone am adorned with this splendid prerogative, but in turns another orator succeeds another each year:
