# sent_id = orat25.1.7
# text = at hoc regnum Friderici Guilelmi auspicia non solum pacatum ab exteris bellis longo ex tempore praestiterunt, sed etiam ad aequabilem quendam rerum deduxerunt statum, motu quidem haud carentem, sed motu gaudentem quieto, in quo, nisi quid acciderit singulare, nihil unum ita emineat, ut in maximis his et sanctissimis sollemnibus ad illud unice dirigi orationem, ex illo omnem peti laudis materiam fas esse videatur.
# reading_translation = But the auspices of this kingdom of Frederick William have not only kept it peaceful from foreign wars for a long time, but have also led it to a certain even state of affairs, indeed not lacking motion, but rejoicing in quiet motion, in which, unless something extraordinary happens, nothing single stands out so much that in these greatest and most sacred solemnities it seems right that the speech be directed uniquely to that one thing, and that all material for praise be sought from it.
