# sent_id = orat25.3.8
# text = quemadmodum olim Anaxarchus Abderites, qui propriam quandam philosophandi viam inierat et commune hominum aspernabatur iudicium, quum Alexandrum Magnum ob necem Cliti illatam summo affectum maerore videret, reprehendit regem, quem universus suspiceret orbis, quod tamquam mancipium lacrimaret proiectus, hominum reverens instituta et metuens vituperia:
# reading_translation = Just as once Anaxarchus of Abdera, who had entered upon a certain peculiar way of philosophizing and scorned the common judgment of men, when he saw Alexander the Great afflicted with the deepest grief because of the murder of Clitus, reproved the king, whom the whole world might admire, because, cast down like a slave, he wept, respecting the institutions of men and fearing reproaches:
