# sent_id = orat25.4.87
# text = ille igitur quum inde a pueritia Graecis Latinisque litteris esset egregie imbutus, nec contemnendam operam in musica et pictura affinibusque artibus posuisset, in summa familiaritate quidem habuit grammaticos, rhetores, philosophos, geometras, musicos, pictores, architectos, et professores omnis generis honoravit opibusque ditavit, sed nimia ambitione, quod doctior videri omnibus volebat, irrisit, illusit, invidia pressit eruditissimum quemque, Apollodorum vero architectum, qui eius diagrammata liberius taxaverat, non solum in exsilium eiecit, sed postremo, qua erat saevitia, etiam occidit.
# reading_translation = He, therefore, since from boyhood he had been excellently imbued with Greek and Latin letters, and had devoted not contemptible effort to music, painting, and kindred arts, indeed held grammarians, rhetoricians, philosophers, geometers, musicians, painters, and architects in the closest intimacy, and honored and enriched professors of every kind, but with excessive ambition, because he wished to appear more learned than all, he mocked, ridiculed, and oppressed with envy every most learned man; and Apollodorus the architect, who had criticized his diagrams rather freely, he not only drove into exile, but finally, with his characteristic cruelty, even killed.
# literal_translation = He therefore since from boyhood with Greek and Latin letters had been excellently imbued, and not contemptible effort in music and painting and kindred arts had placed, in greatest intimacy indeed he had grammarians, rhetoricians, philosophers, geometers, musicians, painters, architects, and professors of every kind he honored and with wealth enriched, but with excessive ambition, because more learned to seem to all he wished, he mocked, ridiculed, with envy oppressed every most learned one, Apollodorus truly the architect, who his diagrams rather freely had criticized, not only into exile he cast out, but finally, with which was cruelty, even killed.
# generator = deepseek-chat
