# text = Postremo precor Deum Optimum Maximum, ut eius principis, cuius auspiciis Borussia per extrema olim discrimina traducta integra est, recreata atque aucta nunc floret, firma et immota stabit posthac, ut Friderici Guilelmi porro provideat saluti, faveatque et perpetuitatem addat beneficiis per illius manus in rem publicam collatis, atque una cum Rege dilectissimo domum Augustam servet incolumem.
# reading_translation = Finally, I pray to God, the Best and Greatest, that, as under the auspices of that prince through whose leadership Prussia, having been led through the greatest dangers of old, has remained whole, and now flourishes renewed and enlarged, so it will stand firm and unmoved hereafter; that He may further provide for the welfare of Frederick William, and may favor and add perpetuity to the benefits conferred through his hands upon the state; and together with the most beloved King, may He keep the Augustan house safe and unharmed.
# literal_translation = Finally I pray God Best Greatest, that of that prince under whose auspices Prussia through extreme formerly dangers having-been-led-through whole is, having-been-renewed and having-been-increased now flourishes, firm and unmoved will-stand hereafter, that of Frederick William further may-provide for welfare, and-may-favor and perpetuity may-add to-benefits through his hands upon the state conferred, and together with King most-beloved house Augustan may-keep safe.
