# sent_id = orat26.1.1
# text = Quum in anniversariis his sollemnibus sanctissimis, quae Regi optimo civium dedicavit pietas, tantum non ab incunabulis scholae nostrae quotannis verba facere solitus, auditores, superiorem annum, quod publicis districtus muneribus eram, intermisissem invitus, et successisset in locum meum collega carissimus, quem tum summa cum voluptate audivimus Friderici Guilelmi laudes eleganter, copiose, graviter disserentem:
# reading_translation = Since, in these most holy annual solemnities, which the piety of the citizens has dedicated to the best King, I have been accustomed to speak almost from the very cradle of our school, and since I had reluctantly omitted the previous year, because I was occupied with public duties, and my dearest colleague had succeeded in my place, whom we then heard with the greatest pleasure discoursing elegantly, copiously, and gravely on the praises of Frederick William:
# literal_translation = When in annual these most-holy solemnities, which to-the-best-King of-citizens dedicated piety, almost from-cradles of-our-school yearly to-speak accustomed, hearers, previous year, because with-public occupied duties I-was, I-had-intermitted unwillingly, and had-succeeded in place my colleague dearest, whom then with-greatest pleasure we-heard of-Frederick-William praises elegantly, copiously, gravely discoursing:
