# sent_id = orat26.1.6
# text = nunc me in beatissima et affluentissima rerum copia frangit et affligit illud ipsum, quo mihi visus eram erigi posse, qui appropinquante iam senio et exhaustis eloquentiae telis, nec pondere sententiarum neque ubertate dicendi nec lateribus ita valeam, ut contendere possim cum fortioribus et integris, quibus cedere malim quam comparari.
# reading_translation = Now, in the most blessed and most abundant abundance of resources, that very thing breaks and afflicts me, by which I had seemed to myself to be able to be lifted up, since, with old age now approaching and the weapons of eloquence exhausted, I am not so strong either in weight of thoughts or in richness of speech or in lungs, that I could contend with stronger and unimpaired men, to whom I would rather yield than be compared.
# literal_translation = Now me in most-blessed and most-abundant abundance of-resources breaks and afflicts that very thing, by which I had-seemed to-be-able to-be-raised, who with-approaching already old-age and exhausted weapons of-eloquence, neither in-weight of-thoughts nor in-richness of-speaking nor in-lungs so-much I-avail, that I-may-be-able to-contend with stronger and unimpaired, to-whom I-would-prefer to-yield than to-be-compared.
