# text = Quodsi mihi obrepserit languor, neque exaequavero priorum annorum alacritatem, transferatis rogo in hoc tempus aliquid eius studii, quo me olim videmini prosecuti esse dicentem, et patiamini pristinae facilitatis vestrae memoria refici meam mentem, quae non refecta sit quiescendo.
# reading_translation = But if weariness should steal upon me, and I should not equal the vigor of previous years, I ask that you transfer to this time some of that zeal with which you once seem to have pursued me as I spoke, and that you allow my mind, which has not been restored by rest, to be refreshed by the memory of your former indulgence.
