# sent_id = orat26.1.8
# text = Quid quod meo iure mihi videor indulgentiam vestram non modo precari sed postulare, quod quo vos prudentiores estis, auditores, eo magis intelligitis, in quantum discrimen committatur is, qui quod Regis laudibus saepissime et per omnes partes perfunctus est, cogatur aut iterandis iis, quae prius dixit, sibi non satisfacere, aut longius discedendo a proposito minus respondere huius diei dignitati et tantae vestrae exspectationi.
# reading_translation = What of the fact that I think I have the right not only to beg but to demand your indulgence, because the more prudent you are, my listeners, the more you understand into what a critical situation he is placed who, having often and in every part performed the praises of the King, is forced either, by repeating what he said before, not to satisfy himself, or, by departing further from his purpose, to respond less to the dignity of this day and to your great expectation?
# literal_translation = What that by-my-right I seem to-myself indulgence your not only to-beg but to-demand, because the more you prudent are, hearers, the more you-understand, into what a-crisis is-committed he, who because the-King's praises very-often and through all parts has-performed, is-forced either by-repeating those-things which before he-said, to-himself not to-satisfy, or by-departing-farther from the-proposed-subject less to-respond to-the-dignity of-this-day and to-so-great your expectation.
