# sent_id = orat26.2.36
# text = Atque huc quum perventum est, simul eum studiorum fructum haud exiguum percipere gens solet, ut non pauci aliqui et insigniores viri litterarum custodes et dispensatores sint, sed auctis comparandae eruditionis subsidiis facilique ad eam aditu dato et vulgata per omnes artis cum aliquo successu tractandae via et ratione, quam invenerant et praeceperant ii, qui familiam duxerunt, eruditio latius sparsa et disseminata sit, multosque nec contemnendos auctores habeat, quorum nullus ita emineat, ut longiori reliquos intervallo superet.
# reading_translation = And when this point has been reached, the nation is accustomed to reap no small fruit of its studies, so that not only are there some distinguished men who are guardians and stewards of literature, but with the resources for acquiring learning increased, with easy access to it provided, and with the method and system of treating every art with some success made known to all, which those who led the way had discovered and taught, learning has been spread and disseminated more widely, and has many authors not to be despised, none of whom so stands out as to surpass the rest by a long interval.
# literal_translation = And to-this-place when it-has-been-arrived, at-the-same-time that fruit of-studies not small to-perceive the-nation is-accustomed, so-that not few some and more-distinguished men guardians and stewards of-literature are, but with-increased resources of-comparing learning and with-easy to-it access given and with-made-known through all arts of-treating with-some success way and method, which had-found and had-taught those, who the-family led, learning more-widely spread and disseminated has-been, and many and-not-to-be-despised authors has, of-whom none so stands-out, that by-longer the-rest interval it-may-surpass.
