# sent_id = orat26.3.8
# text = Quae ars quamquam dici vix potest quantum in rebus publicis momentum habeat, quod libertati parenti suae reddit nutricia, quod latentem civitatium labem aperit publicamque simulationem, quod de imminentibus monet periculis, quod providet, hortatur, incusat, ignaviam pellit, inertes rebusque gerendis impares deprimit et rei publicae gubernaculis admovet prudentissimos, fortissimos, promptissimos:
# reading_translation = Although it can hardly be said how great an influence this art has in public affairs, because it gives back to liberty, its parent, its nurse, because it exposes the hidden decay of states and their public pretense, because it warns of impending dangers, because it provides, urges, reproaches, drives out idleness, depresses the inactive and those unequal to the conduct of affairs, and brings to the helm of the republic the most prudent, the bravest, the most ready:
# literal_translation = Which art although it can hardly be said how great a weight it has in public affairs, because it gives back to liberty its parent its nurse, because it opens the hidden decay of states and public pretense, because it warns of impending dangers, because it provides, urges, reproaches, drives out idleness, depresses the inactive and those unequal to affairs to be done, and to the helm of the republic brings the most prudent, the bravest, the most ready:
# generator = deepseek-chat
