# sent_id = orat26.3.19
# text = Nec vereor idem aliqua ex parte transferre ad historiam, quae primum bene scribi nequit nisi ab eloquente et facundo, quae praeterea eandem fere quam eloquentia libertatem dicendi postulat, quod prima haec historiae lex est, ut non modo nihil falsi dicere audeas, sed quidquid verum est dicere, denique quam refugient et aggredi reformidabunt praeclara ingenia, quum primum perviderint reticenda et premenda esse non quae sibi ipsis, sed quae aliis quibuslibet displiceant iudicibus, et nullo fructu publico conflare sibi invidiam et offensiones, qui nolit vel simulare vel dissimulare.
# reading_translation = And I do not fear to transfer the same thing in some measure to history, which cannot be well written except by an eloquent and fluent writer, which moreover demands nearly the same freedom of speech as eloquence, because this is the first law of history, that you should not only not dare to say anything false, but should say whatever is true, and finally which brilliant minds will flee from and shrink to approach, when they have first perceived that things must be concealed and suppressed not because they displease themselves, but because they displease any other judges whatsoever, and that he who is unwilling either to pretend or to dissemble would incur for himself envy and offenses with no public benefit.
# literal_translation = And I do not fear the same thing in some part to transfer to history, which first well cannot be written except by an eloquent and fluent, which moreover the same nearly as eloquence freedom of speech demands, because this first of history law is, that not only nothing false to say you should dare, but whatever true is to say, finally which will flee and to approach will shrink brilliant minds, when first they have perceived to be concealed and to be suppressed not those things which to themselves, but those which to others whomever displease judges, and with no public fruit to procure for themselves envy and offenses, he who would not wish either to pretend or to dissemble.
# generator = deepseek-chat
