# sent_id = orat27.1.1
# text = Qui inde ab adolescentia, multorum successu annorum continuo, laetissimam eius diei sollemnitatem, quo patriae beandae natus Fridericus Guilelmus est, oratione mea celebravi, viri illustrissimi, doctissimi, commilitones ornatissimi, nunc ultimo officio Patris patriae manibus iusta persoluturum quo me sensu affectum, qua fiducia instructum aggredi putatis ad tantam rem, tam gravem et arduam, tam tristem et lugubrem?
# reading_translation = I, who from my youth, with the continuous success of many years, have celebrated in my speech the most joyful solemnity of that day on which Frederick William was born for the happiness of the fatherland, most distinguished men, most learned men, most honored fellow soldiers, now about to pay the last due to the shades of the Father of the Fatherland with the final office, with what feeling do you think I am affected, with what confidence equipped, to approach so great a matter, so grave and arduous, so sad and mournful?
# literal_translation = I who from youth, with the continuous success of many years, the most joyful solemnity of that day on which for the fatherland to be blessed was born Frederick William, in my speech have celebrated, most distinguished men, most learned, most honored fellow soldiers, now with the last office to the shades of the Father of the Fatherland the due about to pay, with what feeling affected, with what confidence equipped, you think that I approach to so great a matter, so grave and arduous, so sad and mournful?
