# reading_translation = Truly, how great a consolation for such a loss and relief of grief it is, that to the uniquely beloved Prince has succeeded a King of most robust age, distinguished by the most beautiful gifts of mind and talent, equipped with the best arts, whose public and private virtues we have come to know through use and experience and through benefits conferred upon us, whose excellent disposition I would not hesitate even now to celebrate more fully, were it not that an untimely eulogy of a beginning Prince in this common and deepest sorrow would seem to be out of place.
