# sent_id = orat28.1.1
# text = In conventu hoc laetissimo, quem primum hodie agimus, auditores, ut Regis dilectissimi natalicia rite pieque celebremus, non mihi videtur fas esse aliud dicendi exordium sumere nisi ex gratibus Deo Optimo Maximo agendis meo nomine vestroque et rei publicae universae, quod postquam non licet superstitem colere eum principem, ad cuius venerationem totiens nos in hanc curiam convocaverat communis gratulatio et veluti patris caritas, sanctissimo legitimae successionis iure voluerit imperium transferri in Dominum hunc clementissimum, quem difficilius sit non diligere, non laudare, quam intimo affectu diligere, verissima oratione laudare.
# reading_translation = In this most joyful assembly, which we are holding for the first time today, listeners, in order to duly and piously celebrate the birthday of our most beloved King, it does not seem right to me to take any other beginning of speaking except from giving thanks to God, the Best and Greatest, in my own name and in yours and that of the whole commonwealth, because, since it is not permitted to cherish in person that prince to whose veneration the common rejoicing and, as it were, a father's love had so often summoned us into this hall, He has willed that by the most sacred right of legitimate succession the rule be transferred to this most merciful Lord, whom it would be more difficult not to love, not to praise, than to love with deepest affection and to praise with truest speech.
# literal_translation = In assembly this most joyful, which first today we hold, listeners, in order that of the King most beloved the birthday duly and piously we may celebrate, not to me seems right to be another of speaking beginning to take except from thanks to God Best Greatest to be given in my name and yours and of the commonwealth whole, because after not it is permitted surviving to cherish that prince, to whose veneration so often us into this hall had called together common rejoicing and as it were of a father love, by the most sacred of legitimate succession right he has willed the rule to be transferred to Lord this most merciful, whom more difficult it would be not to love, not to praise, than with deepest affection to love, with truest speech to praise.
# generator = deepseek-v4-pro
