# sent_id = orat28.1.4
# text = Adhuc resonant et resonabunt perpetuo non tam auribus nostris quam mentibus illae Regis voces gravissimae, ex commoto effusae pectore egregiorumque testes consiliorum, illae legatorum et populi acclamationes nulla simulationis aut assentationis suspicione notatae, quibus mutua illa caritas, quae patrem beatissimum cum populo suo coniunxerat, confirmata inter successorem atque universas regni provincias omnesque ordines rei publicae, et documentis certissimis ita declarata est, ut orbem terrarum pervagaretur fama praeclarae huius et quae fere sine exemplo est concordiae, ut ad novi sideris ortum omnes gentes converterent oculos, Borussiaeque fidem, felicitatem, robur perspecta haberent etiam increduli, metuerent etiam audaciores:
# reading_translation = Still resound and will resound forever, not so much in our ears as in our minds, those most weighty words of the King, poured forth from a moved heart and witnesses of excellent intentions; those acclamations of the envoys and the people, marked by no suspicion of pretense or flattery, by which that mutual affection, which had joined the most blessed father with his people, was confirmed between the successor and all the provinces of the kingdom and all orders of the state, and was so declared by the most certain proofs that the fame of this illustrious and almost unprecedented harmony spread throughout the world, that at the rising of a new star all nations turned their eyes, and even the incredulous recognized the faith, happiness, and strength of Prussia, and even the bolder ones feared them.
# literal_translation = Still resound and will-resound perpetually not so-much ears our as minds those of-the-King voices most-weighty, from moved poured-forth heart and-of-excellent witnesses intentions, those of-envoys and of-people acclamations by-no of-pretense or of-flattery suspicion marked, by-which mutual that affection, which father most-blessed with people his had-joined, confirmed between successor and all of-kingdom provinces and-all orders of state, and by-proofs most-certain so declared is, that world would-wander-about fame of-illustrious this and which almost without example is of-harmony, that at new of-star rising all nations would-turn eyes, and-of-Prussia faith, happiness, strength perceived would-have even incredulous, would-fear even bolder:
