# sent_id = orat28.1.5
# text = nec si subitus ille calor vel potius ardor et impetus amoris continuari palam non potuit, quidquam remisit amor ipse, sed veluti amnis, qui exundaverat, alveo redditus ripisque inclusus et cohibitus, temperatum ille tenet cursum et aequabili temperamento pollicetur perpetuitatem.
# reading_translation = And if that sudden warmth, or rather ardor and impulse of love, could not be openly continued, love itself relaxed nothing, but like a river that had overflowed, returned to its channel and enclosed and restrained by its banks, it holds a moderate course and promises perpetuity with even temper.
