# sent_id = orat28.2.1
# text = Humanarum rerum omnium regia potestas maxima est et gravissima, plurimisque circumdata curis et immensam requirens perspicacitatem ingenii, bonitatem, industriam, diligentiam, ut rei publicae provideatur commodis et prospiciatur saluti populi ad summam perventuri prosperitatem, ubi rex, cuius ex nutu pendent omnia, sapienter, benigne, strenue, prompte geret res, perituri vel certe magnis laboraturi calamitatibus, si imprudenti, atroci, ignavo, negligenti parebit domino.
# reading_translation = The royal power over all human affairs is the greatest and most serious, surrounded by very many cares and requiring immense keenness of mind, goodness, industry, diligence, so that the interests of the state may be provided for and the safety of the people may be looked after, who are to arrive at the highest prosperity, when the king, from whose nod all things depend, will manage affairs wisely, kindly, vigorously, promptly; but they will perish or certainly suffer great calamities, if they obey an imprudent, cruel, lazy, negligent master.
# literal_translation = Of human affairs all the royal power greatest is and most-serious, and-surrounded-by-very-many cares and immense requiring keenness of mind, goodness, industry, diligence, so-that to-the-state may-be-provided-for the-interests and may-be-looked-after the-safety of-the-people to-highest about-to-arrive prosperity, when the-king, from-whose nod depend all-things, wisely, kindly, vigorously, promptly will-manage affairs, about-to-perish or certainly about-to-suffer great calamities, if to-an-imprudent, cruel, lazy, negligent it-will-obey master.
