# text = Iam in regia vita hoc difficillimum, quod quum eos, quibus rex administris et consiliariis utitur, plerosque omnes non oporteat nisi in singulis generibus excellere et exercitatos esse, rex, qui velit oneri humeris imposito prorsus sufficere, omnes debet rei publicae partes ingenti animo complecti, diversissimarum rerum si non minutissima quaeque, at certe summam tenere, denique haec diversa mente sua ita coniungere et miscere, inde ut veluti ex sonorum varietatibus unus efficiatur concentus.
# reading_translation = Now in royal life this is the most difficult thing: since it is not fitting that most of those whom the king uses as ministers and counselors should excel and be practiced except in individual fields, the king, who wishes to fully bear the burden placed on his shoulders, ought to embrace all parts of the state with a great mind, to grasp, if not every smallest detail of very diverse matters, at least the sum, and finally to join and mix these diverse things with his own mind in such a way that, as from variations of sounds, one harmony is produced.
