# sent_id = orat28.3.4
# text = qui non modo in ipso principio imperii, acceptis gratiosissime quae a primis litterarum et artium collegiis mittebantur legationibus, quam propitius bonis studiis esset, ostendit, et quod longe gratissimum beneficia accipientibus est, ne exspectans quidem donec rogaretur, huius potissimum universitatis reditus lautissime auxit, sed illustrissima Germaniae decora, salariis annuis liberaliter constitutis, huc vocavit, non solum ut suam quisque artem apud nos faceret et doceret, sed etiam ut ipse eorum uteretur praesentia.
# reading_translation = He showed how favorable he was to good studies not only at the very beginning of his reign, when he received most graciously the embassies sent by the first colleges of letters and arts, and, what is by far most pleasing to those who receive benefits, even without waiting until he was asked, he most lavishly increased the revenues of this particular university; but he also summoned here the most distinguished ornaments of Germany, with annual salaries liberally established, not only so that each one might practice and teach his own art among us, but also so that he himself might enjoy their presence.
# literal_translation = Who not only in the very beginning of the reign, having received most graciously the embassies which were being sent by the first colleges of letters and arts, how propitious to good studies he was, showed, and what by far most pleasing to those receiving benefits is, not even waiting indeed until he might be asked, of this especially university the revenues most lavishly increased, but the most distinguished ornaments of Germany, with salaries annual liberally established, here called, not only so that his own each one art among us might practice and teach, but also so that he himself of them might enjoy the presence.
