# sent_id = orat28.3.100
# text = Quodsi litterae tantum eatenus videbuntur magni habendae esse, quatenus vulgaribus vitae utilitatibus et commodis inservire videntur, non mentis luminibus alendis, spernenda sane et philosophia et studia antiquitatis atque una cum his magna reliquae historiae pars ac nescio an aliqua etiam physicarum et mathematicarum disciplinarum erunt:
# reading_translation = But if literature will seem to be held in high regard only insofar as it appears to serve the common utilities and conveniences of life, and not to the nourishment of the mind's lights, then certainly philosophy and the study of antiquity are to be despised, and along with these a great part of the rest of history, and I know not whether also some part of the physical and mathematical disciplines will be [despised].
