# sent_id = orat29.2.2
# text = immo, etsi patria cuiusque cum certa quadam regione coniuncta sit, tamen non hac superficie, his arvis, his montibus silvisque, fluminibus lacubusque, his domibus et tignis atque hoc congestu lapidum, mutis istis et inanimis, quae, ut ait Tacitus, intercidere et reparari promiscua sunt, constitui patriam, sed potius hac societate hominum, in qua nati sumus, individua et quodammodo aeterna, sive eam nationem seu rem publicam vocare placet.
# reading_translation = Indeed, although each person's fatherland is connected with a certain region, nevertheless it is not constituted by this surface, these fields, these mountains and forests, rivers and lakes, these houses and beams, and this heap of stones, those mute and inanimate things, which, as Tacitus says, are liable to fall and be rebuilt indifferently, but rather by this society of men, in which we were born, individual and in a way eternal, whether one prefers to call it a nation or a republic.
# literal_translation = Indeed, although the fatherland of each one may be joined with a certain region, nevertheless not by this surface, by these fields, by these mountains and forests, by rivers and lakes, by these houses and beams and by this heap of stones, by those mute and inanimate things, which, as Tacitus says, to fall and to be repaired are indifferent, is the fatherland constituted, but rather by this society of men, in which we were born, individual and in a certain way eternal, whether it pleases to call it a nation or a republic.
# generator = deepseek-chat
