# text = Et profecto, dum princeps ne ignoret, quod constat non ignorasse Fridericum Magnum, non ignorare Dominum nostrum clementissimum, se quoque civem esse, quis maiore poterit amore patriae incensus esse quam caput rei publicae, ex quo potissimum patriae pendeat salus?
# reading_translation = And indeed, as long as the prince does not fail to know—what is certain that Frederick the Great did not fail to know, and that our most gracious lord does not fail to know—that he too is a citizen, who could be more inflamed with love of country than the head of the state, on whom especially the safety of the country depends?
