# sent_id = orat29.3.34
# text = Proinde quum patriae caritas principisque amor egregie conspirent, hic fere iisdem quibus illa artibus comprobabitur, hoc est non servitio illiberali, sed boni civis virtute, qualem supra significavimus, rectoque usu libertatis, quem nobis non invidet Fridericus Guilelmus Quartus, sed adiuvat atque auget.
# reading_translation = Therefore, since love of country and love of the prince admirably conspire, the latter will be approved by almost the same means as the former, that is, not by illiberal servitude, but by the virtue of a good citizen, such as we have indicated above, and by the right use of liberty, which Frederick William IV does not begrudge us, but rather promotes and increases.
# literal_translation = Therefore since of-fatherland love and of-prince love admirably conspire, this one almost by-the-same means by-which that one will-be-approved, this is not by-servitude illiberal, but of-good-citizen by-virtue, such-as above we-have-indicated, and by-right use of-liberty, which to-us not envies Frederick William Fourth, but aids and increases.
