# text = Etenim quum regna haud pauca ex pluribus composita nationibus sint, iisque diversis lingua et moribus, quum praeterea eiusdem regni provinciae, etsi habitatorum ingenia non tantum differant, ut ii videantur diversarum esse stirpium, tamen quod ex longo tempore plane separatae fuerant, soleant alia ab aliis plus minusve alienatae esse, earumque incolae degeneri cuidam patriae caritati, qui amor provinciae est, indulgere;
# reading_translation = For since there are not a few kingdoms composed of several nations, and these differing in language and customs, and since moreover the provinces of the same kingdom, even if the characters of their inhabitants do not differ so much that they seem to be of different stocks, nevertheless because they had been completely separated for a long time, are wont to be more or less estranged from one another, and their inhabitants to indulge in a certain degenerate love of country, which is love of one's province;
