# sent_id = orat29.3.58
# text = quis non perspicit, ut olim Friderici Guilelmi Tertii, ita nunc Friderici Guilelmi Quarti benignitate et clementia discretas non solum lingua et moribus sed etiam casibus fortunae et desideriis atque exspectationibus nationes, quae imperio Borussico parent, in unum corpus quantum fieri potest copulari, atque illas si non in rebus omnibus, at certe in Regis optimi amore, unanimo conspirare affectu?
# reading_translation = Who does not see that, just as formerly under Frederick William III, so now under Frederick William IV, the nations that obey the Prussian rule, though separated not only by language and customs but also by the chances of fortune and by their desires and expectations, are united, as far as possible, into one body, and that they, if not in all things, at least in love for their excellent King, conspire with one unanimous feeling?
