# sent_id = orat30.1.1
# text = Quae sollemnia memoriae illius diei colendae consecrata sunt, quo die summum numen voluit Fridericum Guilelmum in spem successionis nasci, ut imperii huius incolumitati et dignitati civiumque consuleretur saluti atque opportunitatibus, iis sollemnibus neminem esse vestrum arbitror, auditores omnium ordinum illustrissimi, ornatissimi, quin iudicet nihil esse accommodatius, nihil magis proprium, quam gratiarum actionem, quas Principi clementissimo quum res publica universa, tum haec nostra, quae me oratorem destinavit, litteraria universitas una cum reliquis bonarum artium in hoc regno scholis debet maximas.
# reading_translation = I think that none of you, most distinguished and most honored auditors of all ranks, judges that there is anything more fitting, anything more proper, than the giving of thanks, which the whole commonwealth, and especially this our literary university, which has appointed me as its speaker, together with the other schools of the liberal arts in this kingdom, owes to the most clement Prince, for those solemn rites which are consecrated to the observance of the memory of that day on which the supreme deity willed that Frederick William should be born into the hope of succession, so that the safety and dignity of this empire and the welfare and opportunities of the citizens might be provided for.
# literal_translation = Which solemn rites of the memory of that day of honoring are consecrated, on which day the supreme deity willed Frederick William into the hope of succession to be born, so that of this empire to the safety and dignity and of the citizens to the welfare and opportunities might be consulted, to those solemn rites none of you to be I think, auditors of all orders most distinguished, most honored, but that he judges nothing to be more fitting, nothing more proper, than the giving of thanks, which to the Prince most clement when the commonwealth whole, then this our, which me as speaker appointed, literary university together with the other of the good arts in this kingdom schools owes greatest.
