# sent_id = orat30.1.2
# text = Quod quum reputo ad officium hoc exsequendum duas praecipue iniri vias posse, alteram, ut quaecunque Rex vel inde a capessito imperio, vel uno hoc, qui a proximis superioribus his sollemnibus effluxit, anno egregie fecerit, enumerentur singillatim ac perpendantur, et quantum hinc bonorum in partes rei publicae quaslibet redundarit, data opera explicetur;
# reading_translation = When I consider that two main paths can be taken to carry out this duty, one being that whatever the King has done excellently, whether from the time he took up the government or in this one year that has flowed from the most recent solemnities, should be enumerated individually and weighed, and how much good has flowed from this into any parts of the state should be explained with deliberate effort;
# literal_translation = Which when I consider, for this duty to be carried out, two especially to be entered upon ways to be able, the one, that whatever the King either from the time of having taken up the government, or in this one, which from the nearest previous these solemnities has flowed out, year has done excellently, should be enumerated individually and be weighed, and how much from this of goods into parts of the republic whichever have overflowed, with given effort should be explained;
