# reading_translation = However it may be, no one will deny that, unless the character of the age itself inclines toward a more perfect state of the arts and sciences, this cannot be brought about even by the munificence of princes or by any rewards that may be proposed; and that, to use this example, in the seventeenth century German poets such as Goethe and Schiller later became would not have emerged, even if some Saxon duke had then cultivated poets as recently the noble house of the princes of Weimar cultivated them.
