# sent_id = orat30.3.4
# text = Haec et talia consideranti mihi, ut Rex noster clementissimus egregius omnis elegantiae iudex et artium ac litterarum amantissimus est, novitque quidquid ingeniosum, pulchrum, magnificum est, dignoscere a promiscuo et vulgari, atque eos, qui optima praestant, requirit, invitat, ad sese perducit, imprimis optandum hoc videtur, illum ut largus ingeniorum proventus ne deficiat, quibus possit succurrere munifice, atque ut illi ipsius saeculi indoles et status civitatis copiam faciant bonas artes quaslibet adiuvandi cum fructu, magnanimisque eius consiliis et exspectationi respondeat eventus.
# reading_translation = As I consider these and similar things, since our most merciful King is an outstanding judge of all elegance and a great lover of arts and letters, and knows how to distinguish whatever is ingenious, beautiful, and magnificent from the commonplace and vulgar, and seeks out, invites, and draws to himself those who provide the best things, it seems to me especially desirable that a rich supply of talents should not fail him, so that he may assist them generously, and that the character of his own age and the condition of the state may give him the opportunity to promote any good arts with success, and that the outcome may correspond to his magnanimous plans and expectations.
# literal_translation = These and such-things considering to-me, as King our most-merciful outstanding of-all elegance judge and of-arts and of-letters most-loving is, and-knows whatever ingenious, beautiful, magnificent is, to-distinguish from the-commonplace and vulgar, and those, who the-best provide, seeks, invites, to himself draws, especially to-be-wished this seems, that him a-rich of-talents supply not may-fail, whom he-may-be-able to-assist generously, and that of-himself of-the-age the-character and condition of-the-state opportunity may-make good arts any to-assist with fruit, and-to-his-magnanimous plans and expectation may-answer the-outcome.
# generator = deepseek-v4-pro
