# sent_id = orat30.3.40
# text = mox quum in Gallia repetita essent consilia a Francisco Primo olim capta studiorum humanitatis instaurandi, ac Ludovico Quarto decimo rege esset effectum, ut Parisii iam non cederent Romae Florentiaeque a Mediceis artium et doctrinarum illustratae luminibus, Germaniam afflictam confectamque esse belli tricennalis strage funestissima, viginti exercitibus, nunc victoribus nunc victis, alio post alium depopulationem, solitudinem, vastitatem tantam inferentibus, ut agros vicosque relinquerent aratores, oppida habitatores, deserta, inculta, squalida iacerent omnia:
# reading_translation = Soon after, when in Gaul the plans once conceived by Francis the First for restoring humane studies had been renewed, and under King Louis the Fourteenth it had been brought about that Paris no longer yielded to Rome and Florence, which had been illuminated by the Medici with the lights of arts and learning, Germany was afflicted and exhausted by the most disastrous slaughter of the Thirty Years' War, by twenty armies, now victorious, now vanquished, one after another bringing such depopulation, desolation, and vast ruin that farmers abandoned their fields and villages, inhabitants their towns, and all things lay deserted, uncultivated, and squalid.
# literal_translation = Soon when in Gaul renewed had been the plans by Francis the First once taken of restoring humane studies, and by Louis the Fourteenth king had been brought about, that Paris now not yielded to Rome and Florence by the Medici of arts and learning illuminated with lights, Germany afflicted and exhausted to be by the slaughter of the Thirty Years' War most disastrous, by twenty armies, now victorious now vanquished, one after another depopulation, desolation, vastness so great bringing, that fields and villages would leave farmers, towns inhabitants, deserted, uncultivated, squalid would lie all things:
