# text = Ipse quidem, ubi suadet, ut in Germanicarum vocum formatione aliquid mutetur, quo magis fiant suaves ac sonorae, facete dicit, si Imperator et octo Electores in comitiis Imperii sollemnibus de ea re leges ferrent, animosos Teutonicae barbariei sectatores risu excepturos haec decreta esse et obstrepituros illud:
# reading_translation = Indeed, when he advises that something be changed in the formation of German words, so that they become more pleasant and sonorous, he wittily says that if the Emperor and the eight Electors were to pass laws on this matter in the solemn assemblies of the Empire, the zealous followers of Teutonic barbarism would receive these decrees with laughter and would shout out this:
