# sent_id = orat31.3.6
# text = Haec igitur externa licet partim natura donet, partim parent ingenium, labor, industria, tamen quantum in his rebus pendeat ex imperantium vel bonitate et sapientia vel duritie atque imprudentia, vix ullum regnum declarat luculentius quam hoc Borussicum, in tanta multorum fundorum sterilitate atque inter insolitas calamitates Friderici Guilelmi curis impensis atque indefessis florentissimum, dum aliae civitates solo fertilissimo caelique temperie saluberrima beatae languescunt per pravitatem legum et institutorum.
# reading_translation = Therefore, although external circumstances may partly be granted by nature and partly arise from talent, diligence, and industry, yet scarcely any kingdom shows more clearly how much in these matters depends on the goodness and wisdom or the harshness and imprudence of rulers than this Prussian one, which, amid the barrenness of so many lands and amid unusual calamities, has flourished through the zealous and tireless efforts of Frederick William, while other states, blessed with very fertile soil and a most healthful climate, languish through the wickedness of their laws and institutions.
# literal_translation = These therefore external things although partly nature may-give, partly may-produce talent, labor, industry, nevertheless how-much in these matters may-hang from the-rulers' either goodness and wisdom or harshness and imprudence, scarcely any kingdom declares more-clearly than this Prussian, in the-great barrenness of-many lands and among unusual calamities of-Frederick William by-the-efforts expended and indefatigable most-flourishing, while other states with-soil most-fertile and with-temperateness of-climate most-healthful blessed languish through the-wickedness of-laws and institutions.
