# sent_id = orat31.3.12
# text = Iam vero etsi non possumus sine externorum possessione bonorum vitam bene sustentare, tantum me iudice abest, ut prava ista, quae hac aetate permultos invasit et variis de causis magnopere commendatur, opinio probanda sit, ex qua vel primus huic generi bonorum locus tribuitur, vel ea omissis reliquis prope omnibus unice spectanda sunt, nec quidquam praeter externorum bonorum curam a principe exspectandum et exoptandum, et qui hac re satisfecerit, principalibus satisfacisse officiis videtur;
# reading_translation = Now indeed, although we cannot sustain life well without the possession of external goods, yet in my judgment it is so far from being the case that that perverse opinion, which in this age has invaded very many and is greatly commended for various reasons, should be approved, from which either the first place is assigned to this kind of goods, or they alone, with nearly all others omitted, are to be regarded, and nothing besides the care of external goods is to be expected and desired from a prince, and whoever has satisfied this seems to have satisfied the principal duties;
# literal_translation = Now indeed although we-are-not-able without the-possession of-external goods life well to-sustain, so-much in-my-judgment it-is-absent, that perverse that, which in-this age very-many has-invaded and for-various reasons greatly is-commended, opinion to-be-approved, from which either first to-this-kind of-goods place is-assigned, or they with-others-omitted nearly all alone to-be-regarded are, and nothing besides the-care of-external goods from-a-prince to-be-expected and to-be-desired, and who in-this-thing has-satisfied, to-principal-duties to-have-satisfied seems;
