# sent_id = orat31.3.14
# text = Nimirum qui solo illorum fructu bonorum dignitatem vitae aestimant, fieri non potest quin quotidiana victus facilitate deliniti et huius scilicet felicitatis suae illecebris capti nihil iam pro retinendis, defendendis, recuperandis summis animi bonis audeant, satisque habeant, si ipsis liceat securis ac tutis etiam cum contumelia imperata et facere et sentire, ac servitutem servire indignissimam.
# reading_translation = Of course, those who measure the dignity of life solely by the enjoyment of those goods cannot fail to be soothed by the daily ease of living and captivated by the allurements of this happiness of theirs, so that they no longer dare anything for the sake of retaining, defending, and recovering the highest goods of the mind, and they are satisfied if they themselves are allowed, secure and safe, even with insult, to do and to feel what is commanded, and to endure the most unworthy slavery.
# literal_translation = Of course who by the sole enjoyment of those goods the dignity of life estimate, it cannot happen but that by the daily ease of living soothed and by the allurements of this happiness of theirs captured nothing now for the sake of retaining, defending, recovering the highest goods of the mind they dare, and enough they have, if to themselves it is allowed secure and safe even with insult commanded both to do and to feel, and slavery to serve most unworthy.
# generator = deepseek-chat
