# text = Denique ne ex iis, quas supra proposui, quaestionibus tertiam plane omittam, ita constat principem benignum et sapientem tribuere beneficia, primum ut adhibito iudicio benignitatem suam contineat, nec beneficia magis proiiciat quam det, nec gratiam corrumpat profusione gratiae, praemiorum diminuens pretium;
# reading_translation = Finally, so that I do not entirely omit the third of the questions I proposed above, it is established that a kind and wise prince bestows benefits in such a way that, first, he restrains his kindness by employing judgment, and does not throw away benefits rather than give them, nor corrupt favor by an overflowing of favor, diminishing the value of rewards;
# literal_translation = Finally, lest from those, which above I proposed, questions the third entirely I omit, thus it is established that a prince kind and wise bestows benefits, first so that having employed judgment his kindness he restrains, and not benefits more throws away than gives, nor favor corrupts by profusion of favor, of rewards diminishing the price;
# generator = deepseek-chat
