# sent_id = orat31.3.113
# text = Etenim vir magnus, sapientiae et virtutis et libertatis exemplum, huius universitatis olim decus in paucis insigne, quem maiores natu vidimus ex hoc ipso suggestu fulmina eloquentiae torquentem, in luculenta quadam commentatione hortatur omnes, qui tantae rei pares sint, „ut bellum internecivum indicant primo isti errori, omnium malorum nostrorum ac miseriae fonti venenato, principis esse felicitati nostrae providere, atque ut eum errorem per omnes latebras, per universum scientiae nostrae orbem persequantur, ubiubi delituerit, donec deletus fuerit ex orbe terrarum et in Tartarum reversus, unde emerserit." „Nescimus", inquit, „quibus rebus felicitas nostra adiuvetur;
# reading_translation = For a great man, a model of wisdom and virtue and freedom, once an outstanding ornament of this university among a few, whom we older men have seen hurling thunderbolts of eloquence from this very platform, in a certain brilliant essay urges all who are equal to so great a task "to declare an internecine war first upon that error, the poisoned source of all our evils and misery, that it is the prince's duty to provide for our happiness, and to pursue that error through all its hiding places, through the entire world of our knowledge, wherever it has hidden, until it has been destroyed from the face of the earth and returned to Tartarus, whence it emerged." "We do not know," he says, "by what things our happiness is aided;
# literal_translation = For a man great, of-wisdom and of-virtue and of-freedom a-model, of-this university once an-ornament among few outstanding, whom older by-birth we-have-seen from this very platform thunderbolts of-eloquence hurling, in a-certain brilliant essay urges all, who to-so-great a-matter equal are, "that war internecine they-declare first to-that error, of-all evils our and of-misery source poisoned, of-the-prince to-be for-happiness our to-provide, and that that error through all hiding-places, through the-entire of-knowledge our world they-pursue, wherever it-has-hidden, until destroyed it-has-been from the-world of-lands and into Tartarus returned, whence it-emerged." "We-do-not-know," he-says, "by-which things happiness our is-aided;
# generator = deepseek-v4-pro
