# sent_id = orat31.5.9
# text = Hic uti nunc votis cunctorum viget floretque, ita optamus, ut eius felicitas, quae ab imperii Borussici prosperitate seiungi non potest, firma et imperturbata permaneat, ut generosus eius animus nunquam rebus adversis contristetur, atque ut, quo candore, qua fide, qua caritate suorum ille commodis providet, eodem candore, fide, caritate illius virtutem, quoad summo rei publicae moderatori gratiam referre inferiores possunt, remuneretur populus universus.
# reading_translation = Just as he now thrives and flourishes through the prayers of all, so we pray that his happiness, which cannot be separated from the prosperity of the Prussian state, may remain firm and undisturbed, that his noble spirit may never be saddened by adverse circumstances, and that, with the same candor, faith, and love with which he provides for the interests of his people, the whole people may reward his virtue, insofar as those who are inferior can show gratitude to the supreme ruler of the state.
