# sent_id = orat32.2.20
# text = quamquam concedo, qui has litteras docent, aliquid harum genuinae utilitati detraxisse, quod sapientis monitoris Aristotelis obliti, qui ne musicis quidem usque eo erudiri pueros liberaliter educandos vult, quo usque eum, qui ad artem musicam factitandam instituatur, discipulos coeperunt magis subtilioribus artis praeceptis imbuere, quae grammaticis futuris necessaria sunt, quam veterum auctorum lectione ad humanitatem fingere animos.
# reading_translation = Although I concede that those who teach these letters have detracted something from the genuine usefulness of these studies, because, forgetting the wise admonition of Aristotle, who does not even want boys being liberally educated to be instructed in music to the point where one who is being trained for the practice of the art of music is, they have begun to imbue their students more with the more subtle precepts of the art, which are necessary for future grammarians, than to shape their minds to humanity by the reading of ancient authors.
