# sent_id = orat32.2.38
# text = Iam qui ex gentilium litteris fidei discrimen metuunt, etsi diffido hos meis rationibus vinci vel placari posse, tamen monitos velim, Imperatorem Iulianum Christianis, quo eos affligeret, interdixisse ethnica illa disciplina et institutione, et qui sacra nostra saeculo sexto decimo emendarunt, nulla re magis adiutos esse quam renatis antiquitatis studiis, et qui viri ecclesiae emendationi maxime faverunt atque opitulati sunt, eos fuisse antiquis litteris instructissimos ac politissimos.
# reading_translation = Now those who fear that the Christian faith might be endangered by the literature of the pagans, although I doubt that they can be convinced or appeased by my arguments, nevertheless I should like to warn them that the Emperor Julian, in order to afflict the Christians, forbade them that pagan learning and education, and that those who reformed our sacred rites in the sixteenth century were helped by nothing more than by the revived study of antiquity, and that the men who most favored and supported the reform of the church were those most thoroughly trained and polished in ancient literature.
# literal_translation = Now those who from the literature of the pagans fear a danger to the faith, although I doubt that these can be conquered or appeased by my reasons, nevertheless I should wish them warned, that the Emperor Julian to the Christians, in order that he might afflict them, forbade that pagan discipline and instruction, and that those who corrected our sacred things in the sixteenth century were aided by nothing more than by the revived studies of antiquity, and that the men who to the correction of the church most favored and were helpful, those were in ancient literature most instructed and most polished.
# generator = deepseek-chat
