# sent_id = orat32.2.135
# text = tamen quod ii, qui publici et sacri regiminis gubernabla tenent, litteris ipsi excoluntur et ad res gerendas instituuntur, iussa et placita positiva ex praeceptis scientiae paullatim colorem ducunt, et communis gentium consensus, postquam longo temporis spatio quae sanxerat prava vel certe minus probabilia secutus est, multisque parricidiis in homines sapientissimos et innocentissimos commissis inquinati sunt iudices fanatici, ad meliorem frugem convertitur duce ratione victrice, quam a Deo, ratione summa et absoluta, nobis insitam impie ingratus fuerit qui calumnietur.
# reading_translation = Nevertheless, because those who hold the helm of public and sacred government are themselves cultivated by letters and trained for conducting affairs, the positive commands and decrees gradually take on a color from the precepts of science, and the common consensus of nations, after it has for a long time followed what it had sanctioned as perverse or at least less probable, and after fanatical judges have been stained by many murders committed against the wisest and most innocent men, is converted to a better way of life, with reason as the victorious guide, which reason, implanted in us by God, the highest and absolute reason, he would impiously and ungratefully slander who should calumniate it.
