# text = Vtinam igitur universi operam demus, collegae et commilitones, ut ea, qua schola nostra olim crevit, concordia tum omnium ordinum, qui quod omnes litterarum partes interiori vinculo nexae sunt, antiquo et probato more in unum hoc atque individuum universitatis corpus coniuncti sunt, tum docentium et discentium, tum rei publicae civilis et litterariae, maneat et confirmetur, omnesque remoti ab ambitione et cupiditate qualibet verum bonumque et pulchrum appetamus, sectemur, disciplina et moribus exprimamus!
# reading_translation = Therefore, colleagues and fellow students, let us all strive that the harmony by which our school once grew may remain and be strengthened, both that of all orders, who, because all parts of literature are bound by an inner bond, are united in this one and indivisible body of the university according to the ancient and approved custom, and that of teachers and learners, and that of the civil and literary republic; and let us all, removed from ambition and any desire, seek, pursue, and express in discipline and morals the true, the good, and the beautiful!
# literal_translation = Would-that therefore all we give effort, colleagues and fellow-students, that that, by-which our school once grew, harmony both of-all orders, who because all parts of-literature by-inner bond are-bound, by-ancient and approved custom into-this-one and indivisible of-university body are-united, and of-teaching and of-learning, and of-republic civil and literary, may-remain and be-strengthened, and-all removed from-ambition and desire any the-true and-good and-beautiful let-us-seek, let-us-pursue, by-discipline and morals let-us-express!
