# sent_id = orat32.2.176
# text = Hunc regem ex quo mihi copia fuit quum in aliis conventibus publicis tum ex hoc suggestu orationibus quotannis celebrandi ac venerandi, nunquam non praedicavi illius ingenium optimis artibus et litteris deditum, et non solum eruditionis, sed etiam, quod rarius in principe, eruditorum amorem, denique studia a vulgaribus deliciis et voluptatibus prorsus remota, ad egregium quidvis et honestum et grave et sublime conversa, quibus sicut ipse excellit, ita populos suos eo perfectionis atque laudis evehi cupiat, ut digni populi rege magnanimo, dignus rex populis cultissimis et fidissimis merito habeatur.
# reading_translation = This king, whom I have had the opportunity, both in other public assemblies and from this platform, to celebrate and venerate in speeches every year, I have never ceased to praise for his intellect devoted to the best arts and letters, and not only for his love of learning, but also—what is rarer in a prince—for his love of the learned, and finally for his pursuits entirely removed from common pleasures and delights, turned toward everything excellent, honorable, serious, and sublime; and just as he himself excels in these, so he desires that his peoples be raised to such a degree of perfection and praise that the peoples may deservedly be considered worthy of a great-souled king, and the king worthy of the most cultivated and loyal peoples.
# literal_translation = This king, from whom to me opportunity has been, as in other assemblies public so from this platform with speeches every year to celebrate and to venerate, never not I have proclaimed his intellect to the best arts and letters devoted, and not only of learning, but also, what rarer in a prince, of the learned the love, finally pursuits from common delights and pleasures entirely removed, to excellent anything and honorable and serious and sublime turned, by which as himself excels, so his peoples to that of perfection and of praise to be raised he desires, that worthy peoples of a king great-souled, worthy king of peoples most cultivated and most loyal deservedly be held.
# generator = deepseek-v4-pro
