# text = Tot enim hoc anno insignia in re publica gessit Fridericus Guilelmus, ut qui in his sollemnibus ipsius nomini dedicatis constituerit alia atque haec publica tractare, debeat ineptus videri, atque ut ne eruditus quidem, licet parum versatus in re publica sit, nisi velit doctor plane umbraticus videri, devitare illa possit, quae universorum non modo civium sed hominum animos adverterunt et commoverunt, denique ut ne hoc quidem verendum sit, ne qui de re publica coram adolescentibus dicat, incurrat in reprehensionem.
# reading_translation = For this year Frederick William has performed so many notable deeds in the state that anyone who, in these solemnities dedicated to his name, should choose to treat other matters rather than these public affairs, would have to seem foolish; and that not even a learned man, although he may be little versed in public affairs, unless he wishes to seem a mere closet scholar, could avoid those things which have attracted and moved the minds of all, not only citizens but men; and finally that there is no need to fear that anyone speaking about public affairs before young men should incur reproach.
# literal_translation = For so many this year notable deeds in the state has performed Frederick William, that whoever in these solemnities to his name dedicated should choose other things than these public affairs to treat, ought foolish to seem, and that not even learned, although little versed in public affairs he may be, unless he wishes doctor plainly closet to seem, could avoid those things, which of all not only citizens but men the minds have attracted and moved, finally that not even this to be feared is, that anyone about public affairs before young men speaking should incur into reproach.
