# text = sed quod res publicae communes universorum sunt, non aliena sed sua agit, qui eas ad sese pertinere putat, neque haec communia ab ulla parte civium sine damno communi negliguntur, ac nemo paullo prudentior, quoquo collocatus loco est, debet huius curae plane expers esse.
# reading_translation = But because the affairs of the republic are common to all, he who thinks that they pertain to himself does not act as a stranger but as one concerned with his own affairs, and these common concerns are not neglected by any part of the citizens without common harm, and no one who is even a little prudent, wherever he is placed, ought to be entirely free from this care.
