# reading_translation = Nevertheless, they ought to be imbued with love of country and to be the more inflamed by this flame, the more vehemently youthful minds are carried by ardor to any studies whatsoever, and it is fitting that they be by no means indifferent to those things which may be prosperous or adverse for the state, and especially that they take pains to be instructed in civic learning by a method both philosophical and historical, and learn to judge correctly about public affairs.
