# sent_id = orat33.3.47
# text = Quod siquibus placet, opulentiam non ex solis fundis sed etiam ex mobilibus pecuniis, qui nunc quum maxime nervi rerum sunt, censendam atque insuper primoribus ecclesiae et litteratorum collegiorum legatis aditum ad summum civitatis concilium dandum esse, quoniam de his rebus in utramque partem disputari potest, futuri eas temporis iudicio relinquimus.
# reading_translation = But if some think that wealth should be assessed not only from landed property but also from movable money, which now especially are the sinews of things, and that moreover access to the supreme council of the state should be given to the leading men of the church and the legates of the learned colleges, since on these matters one can argue on both sides, we leave them to the judgment of future time.
